msgid_plural "broken anti-materiel milspec turrets"
msgstr[0] "反器材军用炮塔（损坏）"

#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "broken grenade launcher milspec turret"
msgid_plural "broken grenade launcher milspec turrets"
msgstr[0] "榴弹发射器军用炮塔（损坏）"

#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "wool pillow"
msgid_plural "wool pillows"
msgstr[0] "羊毛枕"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wool pillow'}
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A pillow to rest your head on when sleeping.  This one is made entirely of "
"fluffy wool!"
msgstr "一个睡觉时用的枕头。这款枕头完全由蓬松的羊毛制成！"

#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "Kevlar plate"
msgid_plural "Kevlar plates"
msgstr[0] "凯夫拉片"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'Kevlar plate'}
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"This is a plate of reinforced Kevlar.  It could be used to repair items made"
" of Kevlar."
msgstr "强化凯夫拉片。可以用来修复由凯夫拉制造的物品。"

#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "scute"
msgid_plural "scutes"
msgstr[0] "鳞甲"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'scute'}
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A bony and scaled protrusion harvested from a large reptile.  Such things "
"were used to make handbags before the Cataclysm, but the material is sturdy "
"and protective."
msgstr "一个从大型爬行动物身上采集的骨质和鳞片突起物。 在大灾变之前，这种东西被用来制成手提包，但这种材料坚固耐用，具有保护作用。"

#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "heavy bone"
msgid_plural "heavy bones"
msgstr[0] "重型骨頭"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'heavy bone'}
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A bone harvested from a large animal such as an elephant, or from certain "
"types of zombies.  It is extremely dense and durable for its size, and "
"largely inedible."
msgstr "一个从大象等大型动物或某些类型的丧尸身上采集的骨头。 就其大小而言，它的密度和耐久性都非常高，而且基本上不能食用。"

#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "sharp teeth"
msgid_plural "sharp teeths"
msgstr[0] "尖牙"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'sharp teeth'}
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"Teeth harvested from a carnivore such as a shark, or from certain types of "
"mutant animals.  They are extremely dense and durable for their size, and "
"can very easily cause jagged wounds."
msgstr "一个从鲨鱼等食肉动物或某些变异动物身上获取的牙齿。 与它们的体型相比，这些牙齿非常密集耐用，很容易造成锯齿状伤口。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'empty beehive'}
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A large, enclosed wooden box with multiple sliding frames in it.  With "
"something to attract bees, it can be used to grow a hive."
msgstr "一个带有多个滑动框的大型封闭木箱。放置一些吸引蜜蜂的东西后，它可以用来培育蜂巢。"

#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "shark plush"
msgid_plural "shark plushs"
msgstr[0] "鲨鱼毛绒娃娃"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'shark plush'}
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "A slightly large shark plushie, perfect for cuddles."
msgstr "一个稍大一点的鲨鱼毛绒娃娃，非常适合拥抱。"

#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "locks and keys set"
msgid_plural "locks and keys sets"
msgstr[0] "锁具套装"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'locks and keys set'}
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A set of locks and keys designed to be installed on something you want to "
"keep prying hands away."
msgstr "一套锁具，可安装在您想锁好的物品上，防止他人擅自打开。"

#: data/json/items/handloaded_bullets.json
msgid "blunderbuss slug"
msgid_plural "blunderbuss slugs"
msgstr[0] "火铳独头弹"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'blunderbuss slug'}
#: data/json/items/handloaded_bullets.json
msgid ""
"A prepared blunderbuss shot of a large hunk of metal.  Better for distance."
msgstr "一颗装好的火铳弹，装着一大块金属弹头。适合远距离射击。"

#: data/json/items/handloaded_bullets.json
msgid "blunderbuss shot"
msgid_plural "blunderbuss shots"
msgstr[0] "火铳霰弹"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'blunderbuss shot'}
#: data/json/items/handloaded_bullets.json
msgid ""
"A prepared blunderbuss shot of marbles, pebbles, bearings, basically "
"whatever is at hand.  The homemade pellet spread and number makes up for the"
" shoddy quality."
msgstr ""
"一颗装好的火铳弹，装着玻璃珠，小石子等随手找到的各类杂物。小弹丸的数量和散布稍稍挽救了一下低劣的子弹质量。\n"
"\"这子弹才有末世废土的味道！\""

#: data/json/items/handloaded_bullets.json
msgid "blunderbuss flechette"
msgid_plural "blunderbuss flechettes"
msgstr[0] "火铳镖形弹"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'blunderbuss flechette'}
#: data/json/items/handloaded_bullets.json
msgid ""
"A prepared blunderbuss shot of homemade flechette made out of nails.  Shreds"
" armor."
msgstr "一颗装好的火铳弹，装着钉子自制来的镖形弹丸，可以穿透护甲。"

#: data/json/items/items_holiday.json
msgid "jack o'lantern"
msgid_plural "jack o'lanterns"
msgstr[0] "万圣节南瓜"

#. ~ Use action menu_text for {'str': "jack o'lantern"}.
#. ~ Use action menu_text for {'str': 'battletorch', 'str_pl':
#. 'battletorches'}.
#. ~ Use action menu_text for {'str': 'candle'}.
#: data/json/items/items_holiday.json data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json src/player_activity.cpp
#: src/veh_interact.cpp
msgid "Light"
msgstr "点亮"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': "jack o'lantern"}.
#: data/json/items/items_holiday.json
msgid "You light the candle in the jack o'lantern."
msgstr "你点亮了万圣节南瓜的蜡烛。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': "jack o'lantern"}
#: data/json/items/items_holiday.json
msgid ""
"This is a plastic lantern that is painted to look like a pumpkin with a "
"face.  It has a candle inside it, that can be replaced when burnt down.  It "
"doesn't provide very much light, but it can burn for quite a long time.  "
"You'll need a lighter or matches to light it."
msgstr ""
"这是一个塑料灯笼，涂成了带鬼脸的南瓜的形状。它的内部有一只蜡烛，烧完之后也可以更换。它无法提供多少亮光，但是能够烧很久。你可以用打火机或者火柴点亮它。"

#: data/json/items/items_holiday.json
msgid "spooky jack o'lantern"
msgid_plural "jack o'lanterns"
msgstr[0] "诡异万圣节南瓜"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': "spooky jack o'lantern", 'str_pl': "jack
#. o'lanterns"}.
#: data/json/items/items_holiday.json
msgid "The candle winks out inside the lantern."
msgstr "灯笼内的蜡烛熄灭了。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': "spooky jack o'lantern", 'str_pl': "jack
#. o'lanterns"}
#: data/json/items/items_holiday.json
msgid ""
"There is a thick LED candle inside the pumpkin face.  It doesn't provide "
"very much light, but it can burn for quite a long time.  This candle is lit."
"  The face shifts."
msgstr "这个带鬼脸的塑料南瓜里面有一大根蜡烛。它无法提供多少亮光，但是能够烧很久。它的蜡烛已经点燃，上面的鬼脸随着蜡烛的火焰晃动。"

#: data/json/items/items_holiday.json
msgid "yule wreath"
msgid_plural "yule wreaths"
msgstr[0] "圣诞花环"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'yule wreath'}
#: data/json/items/items_holiday.json
msgid ""
"This decorative wreath can be deployed as furniture to decorate for the "
"winter holidays."
msgstr "这种装饰花环可以作为家具摆放，用于圣诞节的装饰。"

#: data/json/items/newspaper.json
msgid "flyer"
msgid_plural "flyers"
msgstr[0] "传单"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'flyer'}
#: data/json/items/newspaper.json
msgid ""
"A scrap of paper.  It's got stuff depicted on it, and a lot of boring words."
"  The stuff looks neat at least, but they probably don't make it anymore."
msgstr "一张碎纸，上面有一些图案和很多无聊的文字。图案看上去还挺不错，但大概已经不再生产了。"

#: data/json/items/newspaper.json
msgid "survivor's note"
msgid_plural "survivor's notes"
msgstr[0] "幸存者笔记"

#. ~ Description for {'str': "survivor's note"}
#. ~ Description for {'str': 'note'}
#: data/json/items/newspaper.json
msgid ""
"A scrap of paper.  Something's written on it, scrawled in bad handwriting."
msgstr "一张废纸，上面写了些字，但是太潦草了。"

#: data/json/items/newspaper.json
msgid "character sheet"
msgid_plural "character sheets"
msgstr[0] "角色表"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'character sheet'}
#: data/json/items/newspaper.json
msgid ""
"You're fairly certain this is a character sheet for some sort of game, "
"either that or some poor kid's math homework."
msgstr "你几乎可以确定这是一张游戏角色卡片，不然就是某个倒霉孩子的数学作业。"

#: data/json/items/newspaper.json
msgid "newspaper page"
msgid_plural "newspaper pages"
msgstr[0] "报纸"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'newspaper page'}
#: data/json/items/newspaper.json
msgid ""
"A single sheet of newspaper broadsheet.  It is possibly one of the last "
"issues printed before New England was overwhelmed.  No doubt filled with "
"trivial and out-of-date information, who even reads these things anymore?"
msgstr "一张报纸，可能是新英格兰陷落前的最后几期之一。毫无疑问，里面充满了琐碎且过时的信息，还有谁会读这些东西呢？"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'newspaper page'}
#: data/json/items/newspaper.json
msgid ""
"A single sheet of newspaper broadsheet.  It seems to date from several years"
" ago, and you've NO idea how it lasted this long.  No doubt filled with "
"trivial and out-of-date information, who even reads these things anymore?"
