msgid "You turn on the masonry saw."
msgstr "你启动了切砖机。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'masonry saw (off)', 'str_pl': 'masonry saws
#. (off)'}
#: data/json/items/tool/masonry.json
msgid ""
"This is a construction tool for cutting through concrete or other surfaces."
"  It runs on gasoline.  Using this item will cause it to turn on, turning it"
" into a very powerful but unwieldy melee weapon or a terrible chainsaw."
msgstr "一台用于切割混凝土或其他表面的建筑工具。它以汽油为燃料。使用它以将它启动，使其成为非常强大但笨拙的近战武器或是一台糟糕的链锯。"

#: data/json/items/tool/masonry.json
msgid "masonry saw (on)"
msgid_plural "masonry saws (on)"
msgstr[0] "切砖机（开）"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'masonry saw (on)', 'str_pl': 'masonry saws
#. (on)'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/masonry.json
msgid "You turn off the masonry saw."
msgstr "你关闭了切砖机。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'masonry saw (on)', 'str_pl': 'masonry saws
#. (on)'}
#: data/json/items/tool/masonry.json
msgid ""
"This masonry saw is on and making a lot of noise.  Use it to turn it off."
msgstr "切砖机已经启动，发出可怕的噪声。激活它来关闭。"

#: data/json/items/tool/masonry.json
msgid "grinder blade"
msgid_plural "grinder blades"
msgstr[0] "角磨刀片"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'grinder blade'}
#: data/json/items/tool/masonry.json
msgid ""
"A 125mm angle grinder blade.  You could make a powertool with it, or throw "
"it.  Wielding it without sturdy gloves is a bad idea."
msgstr "125mm角磨机刃片。可以拿它做把角磨机，扔出去也可以。边缘锋利，请先戴手套再扔它。"

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "anesthesia kit"
msgid_plural "anesthesia kits"
msgstr[0] "麻醉工具箱"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'anesthesia kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"A kit for inducing anesthesia for surgery, containing specialized canisters "
"with a variety of powerful hypnotic, analgetic, and stimulative drugs.  It's"
" intended for use in specialized medical equipment, and can't be "
"administered manually."
msgstr "一整套用于手术麻醉的工具箱，内含装有各种强力催眠剂、止痛剂及兴奋剂的瓶子。该工具箱设计主要用于专业医疗设备使用，暂时无法直接使用。"

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "autoclave"
msgid_plural "autoclaves"
msgstr[0] "高压灭菌釜"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'autoclave'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"This is an autoclave.  It's useful for sterilizing things like CBMs.  It "
"requires a massive amount of power, so standard batteries will not power it "
"sufficiently.  Examine a non-sterile CBM and mend it to sterilize."
msgstr ""
"这是一个高压灭菌釜，用于消毒CBM之类的物品。启动它需要非常巨大的能量，因此，如果只有标准容量的电池的话它是无法正常工作的。使用以对未消毒的CBM进行消毒。"

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "inhaler"
msgid_plural "inhalers"
msgstr[0] "哮喘吸入器"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'inhaler'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"Albuterol inhaler.  Used in the treatment of bronchospasm, it is a lifeline "
"for people with asthma.  A mild stimulant, it may cause nervousness or "
"tremors."
msgstr "沙丁胺醇吸入剂。用于治疗支气管痉挛，对于哮喘患者非常有用。一种温和的兴奋剂，它可能导致神经过敏或震颤。"

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "RX12 jet injector"
msgid_plural "RX12 jet injectors"
msgstr[0] "RX12 注射器"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'RX12 jet injector'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"The Rivtech RX12 jet injector is a small pistol-shaped device used to inject"
" advanced fast-healing chemicals through the skin without using a needle.  A"
" label on the side warns against using more than two doses per hour."
msgstr ""
"Rivtech RX12 喷射注射器是一种小巧的手枪状装置，用于将先进的快速愈合化学物质无针注入皮肤。旁边的标签上印有每小时使用不得超过两次的警告文字。"

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "scalpel"
msgid_plural "scalpels"
msgstr[0] "手术刀"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'scalpel'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"This is a very sharp knife designed for surgical cutting.  Its small, sharp "
"blade allows for precision strikes in the hands of the skilled."
msgstr ""
"一把小型的，非常锋利的刀具，被广泛应用于各项外科手术中。如果你很擅长近战武器的话，它也会是一件大杀器。\n"
"\"在寂静岭医院工作的护士们用此解剖过无数活人。\""

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "emergency oxygen pack"
msgid_plural "emergency oxygen packs"
msgstr[0] "应急氧气包"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'emergency oxygen pack'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"This is a small tank of compressed medical oxygen with a folding regulator "
"and mask.  Commonly used in emergency situations, it provides immediate "
"relief for asthma attacks or smoke inhalation, and can provide a brief burst"
" of energy."
msgstr "一小罐医用压缩氧，附带调节器和面罩。能够迅速缓解哮喘症状和烟雾吸入损伤，也能让你在短时间内精神满满。"

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "syringe"
msgid_plural "syringes"
msgstr[0] "针管"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'syringe'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "A medical syringe.  Used for administering intravenous drugs."
msgstr "一支医用针筒，可以用来注射海洛因或其他毒品。"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'DNA'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"The DNA sample of some living creature.  This can be used in a cloning vat, "
"together with a sterile artificial womb, to create a copy of the creature."
msgstr "某种生物的DNA样本。它可以与无菌人造子宫一起用于克隆罐，以创造该生物的复制体。"

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "universal growth medium"
msgid_plural "universal growth medium"
msgstr[0] "通用生长介质"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'universal growth medium'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"A heavily processed nutrient liquid, containing the basic building blocks of"
" life.  A genome workstation could take a stored sample off a USB drive, and"
" convert this raw material into viable DNA for cloning."
msgstr "一种经过深度加工的营养液，含有生命的基本构件。基因组工作台可以读取USB驱动器中存储的样本，并将这种原材料转化为用于克隆的活性DNA。"

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "thermometer"
msgid_plural "thermometers"
msgstr[0] "温度计"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'thermometer'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "A plastic thermometer that can read the air temperature."
msgstr "一个塑料的温度计，可以让你知道当前气温。"

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "oxygen tank"
msgid_plural "oxygen tanks"
msgstr[0] "氧气瓶"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'oxygen tank'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"This is tank of compressed medical oxygen with a regulator and mask.  "
"Commonly used in emergency situations, it provides immediate relief for "
"asthma attacks or smoke inhalation, and can provide a brief burst of energy."
msgstr "一罐医用压缩氧，附带调节器和面罩。能够迅速缓解哮喘症状和烟雾吸入损伤，也能让你在短时间内精神满满。"

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "blood draw kit"
msgid_plural "blood draw kits"
msgstr[0] "采血管"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'blood draw kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"This is a kit for drawing blood, including a test tube for holding the "
"sample.  Use this tool to draw blood, either from yourself or from a corpse "
"you are standing on."
msgstr "一成套用于抽血的工具，还有一条可存放血样的试管。你可以用它抽血，至于是抽你自己的，还是其他什么奇怪生物的，随你的兴趣了。"

#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "wrapped radiation badge"
msgid_plural "wrapped radiation badges"
msgstr[0] "辐射侦测徽章（已包装）"

#. ~ Use action menu_text for {'str': 'wrapped radiation badge'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid "Unwrap badge"
msgstr "拆开包装"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'wrapped radiation badge'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"You remove the badge from its wrapper, exposing it to ambient radiation."
msgstr "你从包装里取出了辐射侦测徽章，使其暴露于环境辐射中。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wrapped radiation badge'}
#: data/json/items/tool/med.json
msgid ""
"This is a badge that detects radiation dosage sealed in a radiation-blocking"
" bag.  Use it to remove it from the bag."
msgstr "一块用来检测辐射量的徽章，密闭在防辐射的包装袋中。使用它以将其从包装中取出。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'anvil'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is an enormously heavy block of oddly shaped steel with a chisel-like "
"projection set into the corner.  It's used in most metalworking fabrication "
"recipes."
msgstr ""
"一块非常沉重形状奇特带有锥形突出体的定型钢锭。在大多数金属加工制造流程中都有用到。\n"
"\"在卡通片中通常作为陷阱砸坏人的头。\""

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "bronze anvil"
msgid_plural "bronze anvils"
msgstr[0] "青铜铁砧"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bronze anvil'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a block of oddly shaped bronze with a chisel-like projection set "
"into the corner.  It's used in most metalworking fabrication recipes."
msgstr ""
"一块形状奇特带有锥形突出体的定型青铜锭。在大多数金属加工制造流程中都有用到。\n"
"\"在卡通片中通常作为陷阱砸坏人的头。\""

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "pair of bolt cutters"
msgid_plural "pairs of bolt cutters"
msgstr[0] "老虎钳"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pair of bolt cutters', 'str_pl': 'pairs of bolt
#. cutters'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a large pair of bolt cutters.  You could use them to cut padlocks or"
" heavy gauge wire."
msgstr "一个用于剪断电线的老虎钳，你还可以用它来剪断铁丝网和锁链。"

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "charcoal forge"
msgid_plural "charcoal forges"
msgstr[0] "火炭锻造台"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'charcoal forge'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a portable, charcoal fired, metalworking forge.  If combined with "
"the right tools, you could use this for metalworking, or it could be used to"
" repair metal items."
msgstr "这是一个便携式的使用木炭作为燃料的金属加工锻造工具。搭配适当的工具，你可以用它来加工金属物品，也可以用于修复金属制品。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'charcoal kiln'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A stout metal box used for producing charcoal via pyrolysis; the incomplete "
"burning of organic materials in the absence of oxygen."
msgstr "一个结实的金属箱，利用它可以采用热解法烧炭；即让有机材料在缺氧环境下不完全燃烧以获得炭。"

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "metalworking chisel"
msgid_plural "metalworking chisels"
msgstr[0] "金工凿"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'metalworking chisel'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a short, stout metalworking chisel.  It's used in some metalworking "
"fabrication recipes."
msgstr "一个短，粗壮的金工凿。用于某些金属加工制造的道具。"

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "crucible"
msgid_plural "crucibles"
msgstr[0] "坩埚"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'crucible'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a small metalworking crucible.  It's used in some metalworking "
"fabrication recipes."
msgstr "一个小的金属坩埚。用于某些金属加工制造的模具。"

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "clay crucible"
msgid_plural "clay crucibles"
msgstr[0] "陶坩埚"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'clay crucible'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a primitive metalworking crucible made of clay.  You could use it "
"for metalworking."
msgstr "这是个简陋的陶制金工坩埚，可以用于金属加工。"

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "electric forge"
msgid_plural "electric forges"
msgstr[0] "便携锻造台"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'electric forge'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a portable electric metalworking forge, powered by batteries.  "
"Combined with the right tools, you could use this for metalworking, or it "
"could be used to repair metal items.  With a little mechanical know-how, you"
" could probably even convert it to run directly off a vehicle's power "
"system."
msgstr ""
"这是一个便携式的电动金属加工炉，由电池供电。搭配适当的工具，你可以用它来加工金属物品，也可以用于修复金属制品。只要掌握一点机械知识，你甚至可以将其转换为直接从车辆的能源系统中运行。"

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "hydraulic press"
msgid_plural "hydraulic presss"
msgstr[0] "液压机"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'hydraulic press'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A large, barely portable hydraulic press, that uses a 36kW motor to squash "
"whatever needs squashing.  Do not put your hand in here, it will get "
"squashed.  Can run off heavy-duty batteries, installed to run off a power "
"grid, or mounted on a vehicle."
msgstr ""
"一台大型、几乎不可移动的液压压机，使用36千瓦电机来压碎任何需要被压碎的东西。切勿将手放入其中，否则会被压碎。可由重型电池供电，也可接入电网或安装在载具上。"

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "finished charcoal kiln"
msgid_plural "finished charcoal kilns"
msgstr[0] "炭窑（完成）"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'finished charcoal kiln'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A charcoal kiln that has finished burning.  Disassemble it to retrieve the "
"charcoal and kiln."
msgstr "一只完成燃烧的炭窑。拆解它以回收木炭和窑炉。"

#. ~ Use action menu_text for {'str': 'filled charcoal kiln'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "Light wood"
msgstr "点燃木头"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'filled charcoal kiln'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "You light the wood."
msgstr "你点燃了木头。"

#. ~ Use action need_fire_msg for {'str': 'filled charcoal kiln'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "You need something to light it with!"
msgstr "你需要点火工具！"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'filled charcoal kiln'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"A kiln filled with wood which will become charcoal after a slow period of "
"burning."
msgstr "一只填满木材的炭窑，木材经过缓慢燃烧后将会变成木炭。"

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "lit charcoal kiln"
msgid_plural "lit charcoal kilns"
msgstr[0] "炭窑（点燃）"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'lit charcoal kiln'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"The kilns embers have died out, you can now disassemble it to harvest the "
"charcoal."
msgstr "炭窑余烬已经熄灭了。拆解它以回收木炭和窑炉。"

#. ~ Use action not_ready_msg for {'str': 'lit charcoal kiln'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "The kiln is still burning."
msgstr "这个窑仍然在燃烧。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'lit charcoal kiln'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "A kiln full of wood that has been lit; better drop it!"
msgstr "装满木材的制炭窑炉，已经点燃了，你最好把它放下。"

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "chainmail sheet"
msgid_plural "chainmail sheets"
msgstr[0] "锁环网"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'chainmail sheet'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a sheet of riveted chainmail.  With some skill, several of these "
"sheets could be connected to make effective armor."
msgstr "一片铆接而成的锁环网。稍有技巧的人，能够用几片锁环网拼接成可用的护甲。"

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "swage and die set"
msgid_plural "swage and die sets"
msgstr[0] "锻造模具"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'swage and die set'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"These are a set of swages and dies for metalsmithing.  These loops and metal"
" blocks are used in some metalworking fabrication recipes."
msgstr "一组用于加工模具的型砧。用于某些金属加工制造的模具。"

#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "pair of metal tongs"
msgid_plural "pairs of metal tongs"
msgstr[0] "铁钳"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pair of metal tongs', 'str_pl': 'pairs of metal
#. tongs'}
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid ""
"These are long, metal tongs.  They are commonly used for cooking or in "
"metalworking fabrication recipes."
msgstr "长颈的铝制火钳。是烹饪或金属加工制造的常用工具。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "compressed air horn"
msgid_plural "compressed air horns"
msgstr[0] "压缩气体喇叭"

#. ~ Use action noise_message for {'str': 'compressed air horn'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "HOOOOONK!"
msgstr "嘟～～嘟～～嘟嘟！"

#. ~ Use action use_message for {'str': 'compressed air horn'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You honk your airhorn."
msgstr "你按下空气喇叭！"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'compressed air horn'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a small can of compressed air attached to a plastic horn.  Pressing "
"the button on top causes it to emit a loud honking sound."
msgstr "这罐压缩空气被安上了一个塑料的号角，只要轻轻按下罐子上的按钮，就会发出巨大的喇叭声。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "alarm clock"
msgid_plural "alarm clocks"
msgstr[0] "闹钟"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'alarm clock'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"A wind-up alarm clock.  Though the noise it makes is unpleasant to wake up "
"to, it's always good to get an early start to your day.  Can also be "
"disassembled into some useful parts."
msgstr "一个发条闹钟。被吵醒实在是不舒服，但起早总没什么坏处。也可以拆成有用的零件。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "cow bell"
msgid_plural "cow bells"
msgstr[0] "牛铃"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'cow bell'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "A brass cow bell.  You feel like you need more of it."
msgstr "一个黄铜牛铃。你觉得你需要更多。（注：Need more cowbell meme）"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid "dab pen"
msgid_plural "dab pens"
msgstr[0] "笔形电子烟"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'dab pen'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You turn on the dab pen."
msgstr "你打开了笔形电子烟。"

#. ~ Use action need_charges_msg for {'str': 'dab pen'}.
#. ~ Use action need_charges_msg for {'str': 'dab pen (on)', 'str_pl': 'dab
#. pens (on)'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json data/json/obsoletion/items.json
msgid "The dab pen's batteries need more charge."
msgstr "笔形电子烟没电了。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'dab pen'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"A battery operated dab pen used for smoking cannabis distillate cartridges."
msgstr "一根用电池供电的笔形电子烟，可以用来吸食大麻精油。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "Cube of Shame"
msgid_plural "Cube of Shame"
msgstr[0] "耻辱立方"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str_sp': 'Cube of Shame'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You inject yourself into the Cube of Shame."
msgstr "你将自己注射进耻辱立方。"

#. ~ Use action need_charges_msg for {'str_sp': 'Cube of Shame'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "Batteries not included."
msgstr "没有装电池。"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Cube of Shame'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a debug-only item for testing relic properties, powered by "
"batteries.  Turn it on to lose intelligence and perception, but gain "
"clairvoyance."
msgstr "这是一个调试用的测试神器的物品。给它装上电池然后打开会降低你的智力和感知，但是获得透视。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "Cube of Shame (on)"
msgid_plural "Cube of Shame (on)"
msgstr[0] "耻辱立方（开）"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str_sp': 'Cube of Shame (on)'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You extract yourself from the Cube of Shame."
msgstr "你将自己从耻辱立方抽出。"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Cube of Shame (on)'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a debug-only item for testing relic properties, powered by "
"batteries.  Drop it or turn it off to retrieve your mind."
msgstr "这是一个调试用的测试神器的物品。丢下或者把它关掉以恢复心智。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "Trapezohedron of Edginess"
msgid_plural "Trapezohedron of Edginess"
msgstr[0] "急躁的偏方三八面体"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Trapezohedron of Edginess'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a debug-only item for testing enchantment mutations.  Wield it to "
"stay up all night, become stealthy, and to see in the dark."
msgstr "这是一个调试用的测试附魔变异的物品。拿着它就可以不知疲倦，行动隐秘且能夜视。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "entrenching tool"
msgid_plural "entrenching tools"
msgstr[0] "工兵铲"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'entrenching tool'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a stout collapsible spade.  It's commonly used by military forces "
"and favored by hikers for digging.  This was a popular weapon during WW1."
msgstr "这是一把结实的可折叠铁锹。它通常被军事部队使用，现在也被徒步旅行者用来挖掘。在第一次世界大战期间十分流行。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "etched human skull"
msgid_plural "etched human skulls"
msgstr[0] "铭刻头骨"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'etched human skull'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "This is a human skull with strange etchings covering it."
msgstr "这是一个雕刻着奇怪刻印的人的头骨。还是回去交任务吧。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "flammable arrow"
msgid_plural "flammable arrows"
msgstr[0] "燃烧箭"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'flammable arrow'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This arrow has a rag soaked in a flammable liquid wrapped around the shaft "
"near the head.  You need to light it before shooting."
msgstr "箭头附近的箭杆上有易燃液体浸泡过的布条缠绕，在发射前，点燃它吧。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "fur rollmat"
msgid_plural "fur rollmats"
msgstr[0] "毛绒卷毯"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'fur rollmat'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You unroll the fur mat and lay it on the ground."
msgstr "你展开毛皮垫子，把它平铺在地上。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'fur rollmat'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a bedroll made of pelts which can be rolled up for transport.  It "
"insulates you from the floor, making it easier to sleep.  Use it to unroll "
"and place on the ground."
msgstr "一床皮毛制成的铺盖，可以卷起来随身携带。垫在地上，让你更容易入睡。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "grappling hook"
msgid_plural "grappling hooks"
msgstr[0] "抓钩"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'grappling hook'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"A folding grappling hook attached to a stout 30-foot long piece of "
"lightweight cord.  Useful for keeping yourself safe from falls.  Can be used"
" in place of a long rope for butchering, in a pinch."
msgstr "可折叠的精钢抓钩，系在一根30英尺长的尼龙绳上。有效保护你从高处落下时的安全。足以吊起大型尸体以便屠宰。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "grip hook"
msgid_plural "grip hooks"
msgstr[0] "挂肉钩"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'grip hook'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "A simple steel meathook with a circular steel handle."
msgstr "一个简单钢制挂肉钩，带有个环形的钢把手。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "hand pump"
msgid_plural "hand pumps"
msgstr[0] "打气筒"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'hand pump'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "This pump is suitable for pumping air into inflatable objects."
msgstr "一个打气筒，可以给任何物体充入空气，比如娃娃。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "bicycle horn"
msgid_plural "bicycle horns"
msgstr[0] "自行车铃"

#. ~ Use action use_message for {'str': 'bicycle horn'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You honk the bicycle horn."
msgstr "你按了下自行车铃。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bicycle horn'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a simple bulb horn, found on many bicycles.  Use to honk.  Honk "
"honk."
msgstr "一个简单的小铃铛，许多自行车上都可以看到。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "truck horn"
msgid_plural "truck horns"
msgstr[0] "卡车喇叭"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'truck horn'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "This is a very loud horn, usually found on large trucks like semis."
msgstr "一个非常响亮的喇叭，通常用在拖车这样的大卡车上。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "ship air horn"
msgid_plural "ship air horns"
msgstr[0] "船用气喇叭"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'ship air horn'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"An enormous ship air horn, extremely loud and deafening.  Usually found on "
"large vessels."
msgstr "一个巨大的船用气喇叭，声音极其响亮，震耳欲聋。通常在大型船舶上可以找到。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "car horn"
msgid_plural "car horns"
msgstr[0] "汽车喇叭"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'car horn'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "This is a car horn meant to be attached to a car's electrical system."
msgstr "汽车喇叭要连接到汽车的电气系统。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "large space heater"
msgid_plural "large space heaters"
msgstr[0] "大型空间加热器"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'large space heater'}.
#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'small space heater'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You turn on the heater."
msgstr "你打开加热器。"

#. ~ Use action need_charges_msg for {'str': 'large space heater'}.
#. ~ Use action need_charges_msg for {'str': 'small space heater'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "The heater needs more charge."
msgstr "加热器没电了。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'large space heater'}
#. ~ Description for {'str': 'large space heater (on)', 'str_pl': 'large space
#. heaters (on)'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"A portable electric heater that steadily emits warm air.  Raises temperature"
" about 10 degrees C and fills a larger volume of air than the smaller "
"version."
msgstr "一种便携式电加热器，能稳定地放出温暖的空气。将温度升高约10℃，并比小型版本排气量更大。"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'large space heater (on)', 'str_pl': 'large
#. space heaters (on)'}.
#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'small space heater (on)', 'str_pl': 'small
#. space heaters (on)'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You turn off the heater."
msgstr "你关闭加热器。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "lifestraw"
msgid_plural "lifestraws"
msgstr[0] "生命饮管"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'lifestraw'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"Set the lifestraw in suspect water, let sit for one minute then drink.  The "
"two part filtration system will purify the water you drink.  Water taken "
"from uncertain sources like a river may be dirty."
msgstr "将生命饮管放入污水中，静置一分钟之后即可饮用。它内置的双重过滤系统将会将水净化至可饮用状态。从河流之类的不明水源取得的水有可能被污染。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "mind splicer kit"
msgid_plural "mind splicer kits"
msgstr[0] "意识连接工具套"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'mind splicer kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"Surgical forceps, cables and a modified smartphone inside a small plastic "
"pouch.  Assembled to steal the mind of some poor man, these are tools of the"
" creepy high-tech sandman."
msgstr "外科手术钳、链接电缆和一个小型智能手机一起被放在了一个塑料袋里面。这件可怕的工具在可怜的人们睡眠的时候可以窃取他的思维。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "permanent marker"
msgid_plural "permanent markers"
msgstr[0] "记号笔"

#. ~ Use action gerund for {'str': 'permanent marker'}.
#. ~ Use action gerund for {'str': 'survival marker'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "Written"
msgstr "写"

#. ~ Use action verb for {'str': 'permanent marker'}.
#. ~ Use action verb for {'str': 'survival marker'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "Write"
msgstr "写"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'permanent marker'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a King Size(tm) industrial strength permanent marker, about halfway "
"between a typical marker and a can of spray paint in size.  Use it to write "
"something down.  However, writing \"Elbereth\" probably won't help you."
msgstr ""
"特大号商标的工业级强度记号笔，大小介于一般的记号笔和喷涂罐之间。可以用它来写东西。但是写下\"Elbereth\"不会有什么用。（注：Elbereth是NetHack中驱赶怪物的咒语）"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "zombie pheromone"
msgid_plural "zombie pheromones"
msgstr[0] "丧尸信息素"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'zombie pheromone'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a disgusting ball of rotting meat of zombie origin.  Squeezing this "
"gland causes a small cloud of pheromones to spray into the air.  Apparently "
"the foul secretion can change zombies' attitude towards you, and they may "
"ignore you for a short period of time.  Perhaps they briefly consider you as"
" one of them."
msgstr ""
"包含着丧尸源质的烂肉球，挤压它会喷射一小团信息素到空气中。这种肮脏的分泌物可以改变丧尸对你的态度，使他们在短时间内无视你，可能它们暂时把你当成了同类。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "pocket watch"
msgid_plural "pocket watches"
msgstr[0] "怀表"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pocket watch', 'str_pl': 'pocket watches'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"An old-fashioned pocket watch.  This one tells you the time and looks good "
"doing it.  Can also be disassembled into some useful parts."
msgstr "一个经典款怀表，可以让你在查看时间时显得很有派头。可以被拆解成零件。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "rollmat"
msgid_plural "rollmats"
msgstr[0] "卷毯"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'rollmat'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You unroll the mat and lay it on the ground."
msgstr "你展开垫子，把它平铺在地上。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'rollmat'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a sheet of foam which can be rolled tightly for storage.  It "
"insulates you from the floor, making it easier to sleep.  Use it to unroll "
"and place on the ground."
msgstr "一大张卷起来的泡沫塑料，很方便存放的样子，如果铺开也能当做一个床铺来使用。使用它以展开。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "safe deposit box"
msgid_plural "safe deposit boxes"
msgstr[0] "保险箱"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'safe deposit box', 'str_pl': 'safe deposit
#. boxes'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a secure combination lock box.  Sadly, you don't know the "
"combination.  Breaking inside it would destroy anything of value."
msgstr "一个组合式锁箱，不幸的是，你不知道密码。强行打开的话会破坏里头值钱的东西。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "sarcophagus access code"
msgid_plural "sarcophagus access codes"
msgstr[0] "危险品开启密码"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'sarcophagus access code'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This printout is a string of numbers to access the elevator in the hazardous"
" waste sarcophagus."
msgstr "一串密码，用来启动通往危险废品储存间的电梯。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "small space heater"
msgid_plural "small space heaters"
msgstr[0] "小型空间加热器"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'small space heater'}
#. ~ Description for {'str': 'small space heater (on)', 'str_pl': 'small space
#. heaters (on)'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"A portable electric heater that steadily emits warm air.  Raises temperature"
" about 10 degrees C."
msgstr "一种便携式电加热器，能稳定地放出温暖的空气。将温度升高约10℃。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "small space heater (on)"
msgid_plural "small space heaters (on)"
msgstr[0] "小型空间加热器（开）"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "spray can"
msgid_plural "spray cans"
msgstr[0] "喷涂罐"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'spray can'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a spray can, filled with paint.  Use this tool to make graffiti on "
"the floor."
msgstr "装满油漆的喷雾罐。可以用来在地面上涂鸦。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'stepladder'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "This is a wooden stepladder.  Use it to set it down."
msgstr "这是一把木制梯子。使用它来放下梯子。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "survival marker"
msgid_plural "survival markers"
msgstr[0] "生存记号笔"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'survival marker'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a sharpened piece of charcoal that is almost guaranteed to make your"
" hands all covered in charcoal.  Use it to write something down."
msgstr "只是一块被磨尖的木炭，你为了磨它，弄得整个手都是木炭黑。使用它来写字。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "survivor telescope"
msgid_plural "survivor telescopes"
msgstr[0] "幸存者望远镜"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'survivor telescope'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"A homemade collapsible telescope.  Too large and inaccurate to use as a "
"weapon scope, but carrying this item in your inventory will double the "
"distance that is mapped around you during your travels."
msgstr "一个自制的可折叠式望远镜，相比军用望远镜更大而且更不准，但有了它，你就能望向很远的地方。放在包里随身携带，大地图从此不再迷茫。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "tear gas payload"
msgid_plural "tear gas payloads"
msgstr[0] "催泪弹载体"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'tear gas payload'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "You pull the pin on the payload."
msgstr "你拉开了催泪弹载体的拉环。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'tear gas payload'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a dummy item used by tear gas hacks.  You should never see it "
"outside of debug."
msgstr "这是被催泪弹无人机使用的虚拟物品，你不应该在调试模式之外的地方看到它。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "active tear gas payload"
msgid_plural "active tear gas payloads"
msgstr[0] "催泪弹载体（激活）"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'active tear gas payload'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a dummy item used by tear gas hacks that just so happens to be "
"counting down.  You should never see it outside of debug."
msgstr "这是被催泪弹无人机使用的虚拟物品，已激活且正在倒计时。你不应该在调试模式之外的地方看到它。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "telescoping umbrella"
msgid_plural "telescoping umbrellas"
msgstr[0] "折叠伞"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'telescoping umbrella'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"A telescoping umbrella which collapses down for easy storage, useful for "
"keeping dry when wielded."
msgstr "一把可伸缩的折叠伞，收起来之后便于携带，拿在手里就不那么容易被淋湿。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "Flaming Chunk of Steel +2"
msgid_plural "Flaming Chunks of Steel +2"
msgstr[0] "燃烧钢块+2"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'Flaming Chunk of Steel +2', 'str_pl': 'Flaming
#. Chunks of Steel +2'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "HOLY SHIT THIS THING IS ON FIRE"
msgstr "我 的 天 啊！ 着 火 啦 ！！"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "Whistle of Tindalos"
msgid_plural "Whistles of Tindalos"
msgstr[0] "廷达罗斯之哨"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'Whistle of Tindalos', 'str_pl': 'Whistles of
#. Tindalos'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "Who is this Tindalos guy?"
msgstr "廷达罗斯是谁？"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "umbrella"
msgid_plural "umbrellas"
msgstr[0] "雨伞"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'umbrella'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "An umbrella with a pointy end, useful for keeping dry when wielded."
msgstr "头部尖尖的伞，握住它有利于保证不被雨淋湿。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "vortex stone"
msgid_plural "vortex stones"
msgstr[0] "漩涡石"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'vortex stone'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This is a stone with spirals all over it, and holes around its perimeter.  "
"Though it is fairly large, it weighs next to nothing.  Air seems to gather "
"around it."
msgstr "一块遍布漩涡刻痕的石头，四周遍布着孔洞。虽然看上去不小，但几乎没有重量，似乎有气流聚集在这块石头的周围。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "whistle multitool"
msgid_plural "whistle multitools"
msgstr[0] "多功能口哨"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'whistle multitool'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"A cheap gadget combining a whistle, thermometer, magnifying glass, and "
"compass."
msgstr "一个廉价的小玩意儿，结合了口哨，温度计，放大镜，和指南针。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "handmade pocket watch"
msgid_plural "handmade pocket watches"
msgstr[0] "自制怀表"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'handmade pocket watch', 'str_pl': 'handmade
#. pocket watches'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"An old-fashioned pocket watch, useful for telling the time and not much "
"else."
msgstr "老式怀表，只能用来报时，其他用处不大。"

#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "artificial womb"
msgid_plural "artificial wombs"
msgstr[0] "人造子宫"

#. ~ Use action friendly_msg for {'str': 'artificial womb'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "The cloned creature seems to enjoy your presence."
msgstr "克隆生物似乎很喜欢你的陪伴。"

#. ~ Use action hostile_msg for {'str': 'artificial womb'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "The cloned creature seems aloof to you!"
msgstr "克隆生物似乎对你很冷淡！"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'artificial womb'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"This artificial womb holds a nearly fully grown clone, nurtured from "
"extracted DNA within a cloning vat.  Activate it, and the organism will "
"swiftly complete its development and emerge ready to function.  Ideal for "
"quickly repopulating herds, restoring endangered species, or deploying "
"engineered creatures with minimal wait."
msgstr ""
"这个人造子宫里装着一个几乎完全长成的克隆体，是在克隆罐中利用提取的DNA培育出来的。激活它，有机体将迅速完成发育并破壳而出，准备投入运作。这是快速重建畜群、恢复濒危物种或部署工程生物且无需久候的理想选择。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'artificial womb'}
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid ""
"A single-use vessel for transporting clones safely from the cloning vat to "
"the field.  Currently empty, if sufficiently sterile it can be used by a "
"cloning vat to grow a creature from a viable DNA sample. "
msgstr "一种用于将克隆体从克隆罐安全运输到野外的一次性容器。目前是空的，如果足够无菌，克隆罐可以使用它通过活性DNA样本来培育生物。"

#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "banjo"
msgid_plural "banjos"
msgstr[0] "斑鸠琴"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'banjo'}
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "A standard factory-made banjo.  Looks to be in working condition."
msgstr "一把批量生产的斑鸠琴，看起来保存的挺不错的。"

#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "bone flute"
msgid_plural "bone flutes"
msgstr[0] "骨笛"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bone flute'}
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "A polished bone flute with five finger holes."
msgstr "一根经过精心打磨的骨笛，上面有着五个音孔。"

#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "wooden flute"
msgid_plural "wooden flutes"
msgstr[0] "木笛"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wooden flute'}
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "A simple flute carved from wood with five finger holes."
msgstr "这是一种用木头雕刻而成的简易长笛，有五个指孔。"

#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "clarinet"
msgid_plural "clarinets"
msgstr[0] "黑管"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'clarinet'}
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "An ornate clarinet made from wood."
msgstr "一只木制的管乐器。"

#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "flute"
msgid_plural "flutes"
msgstr[0] "短笛"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'flute'}
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "A simple silver-plated flute."
msgstr "一只简易的银质短笛。"

#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "trumpet"
msgid_plural "trumpets"
msgstr[0] "短号"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'trumpet'}
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "A brass trumpet with only a few dents here and there."
msgstr "一只黄铜制成的短号，仅仅有些擦伤。"

#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "ukulele"
msgid_plural "ukuleles"
msgstr[0] "四弦琴"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'ukulele'}
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "A small factory made ukulele.  Looks to be in working condition."
msgstr "一把批量生产的四弦琴，看起来保存的挺不错的。"

#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "violin"
msgid_plural "violins"
msgstr[0] "小提琴"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'violin'}
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid ""
"A cheap, factory-made violin with a built-in holder for a bow.  Still "
"produces a nice sound."
msgstr ""
"一把便宜的、工厂批量生产的小提琴，能弹出美妙动听的音乐。\n"
"\"拉的不如弹得好听。\""

#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "golden fiddle"
msgid_plural "golden fiddles"
msgstr[0] "金色小提琴"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'golden fiddle'}
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid ""
"A shiny golden fiddle, with a strange aura around it.  You feel like it once"
" belonged to the best there's ever been."
msgstr "一把闪闪发光的金色小提琴，被某种奇怪的光环环绕着。你有种这玩意曾经属于某个伟人的感觉。"

#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid "chicken cage"
msgid_plural "chicken cages"
msgstr[0] "鸡笼"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'chicken cage'}
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid ""
"A wire container made for transporting chickens, but you can use it to hold "
"any tiny animal.  Use it on a suitable animal to capture, use it on an empty"
" tile to release."
msgstr "一个铁丝网制成的笼子，本来是用来抓鸡的，但也可以用来运输体型类似的动物。激活它后选择需要捕获的动物，或者选择空地放出笼中动物。"

#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid "dog whistle"
msgid_plural "dog whistles"
msgstr[0] "狗哨"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'dog whistle'}
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid ""
"This is a small whistle.  When used, it produces a high tone that causes "
"nearby friendly dogs to either follow you closely and stop attacking, or "
"start attacking enemies if they are currently docile."
msgstr "一只小型的哨子，吹它的时候会产生一种高频的声波，让附近所有非敌对状态的狗狗都会向你靠拢并为你而战。"

#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid "shears"
msgid_plural "shears"
msgstr[0] "大剪刀"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'shears'}
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid "This is a set of shears designed to obtain wool from sheep."
msgstr "这是一把用来剪羊毛的剪刀。"

#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid "electric shears"
msgid_plural "electric shears"
msgstr[0] "电动剪"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'electric shears'}
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid "These electric shears can be used to shear animals quicker."
msgstr "这把电动剪可以更快的给动物剪毛。"

#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid "horse tack"
msgid_plural "horse tacks"
msgstr[0] "鞍具"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'horse tack'}
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid ""
"A saddle, bridle, and associated tack that can be placed on a tamed animal "
"that is capable of being ridden."
msgstr "一个鞍座，一副缰绳，以及配套的各类马钉，能够装在已驯服的动物身上，让它供你骑乘。"

#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid "pet carrier"
msgid_plural "pet carriers"
msgstr[0] "宠物笼"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pet carrier'}
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid ""
"A plastic container meant to hold pets for transport.  Use it on a suitable "
"animal to capture, use it on an empty tile to release."
msgstr "一个塑料笼子，可以用来运输小型宠物。激活它后选择需要捕获的动物，或者选择空地放出笼中动物。"

#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid "wooden pet carrier"
msgid_plural "wooden pet carriers"
msgstr[0] "木制宠物笼"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wooden pet carrier'}
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid ""
"A wooden container meant to hold pets for transport.  Use it on a suitable "
"animal to capture, use it on an empty tile to release."
msgstr "一个木制笼子，可以用来运输小型宠物。激活它后选择需要捕获的动物，或者选择空地放出笼中动物。"

#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid "wooden dog whistle"
msgid_plural "wooden dog whistles"
msgstr[0] "木制狗哨"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wooden dog whistle'}
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid ""
"This is a whistle carved out of hardwood.  When used, it produces a high "
"tone that causes nearby friendly dogs to either follow you closely and stop "
"attacking, or start attacking enemies if they are currently docile."
msgstr "一只硬木雕成的哨子，吹它的时候会产生一种高频的声波，让附近所有非敌对状态的狗狗都会向你靠拢并为你而战。"

#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid "radio car base"
msgid_plural "radio car bases"
msgstr[0] "遥控玩具车盒"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'radio car base'}
#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid "Generic radio car kit, you shouldn't see this."
msgstr "一份抽象化的遥控玩具车盒，你不该在游戏里看到它。"

#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid "radio car box"
msgid_plural "radio car boxes"
msgstr[0] "遥控玩具车盒"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'radio car box', 'str_pl': 'radio car boxes'}
#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid ""
"An RC car, with radio-control and batteries included!  Disassemble to unpack"
" and enjoy."
msgstr "一个遥控车套装，包含无线控制器，还有配套用地电池！拆解它来打开包装并使用。"

#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid "RC control"
msgid_plural "RC controls"
msgstr[0] "无线控制器"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'RC control'}
#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid ""
"A remote control for RC cars, with joystick to steer the car and colorful "
"buttons that don't seem to do anything.  Perhaps they were for the deluxe "
"model?"
msgstr "一个用来操纵遥控车的无线控制器，通过摇杆来控制车的移动，还有一堆用不到的按钮，或许是用来控制更高级的型号的。"

#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid "RC car"
msgid_plural "RC cars"
msgstr[0] "遥控车"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'RC car'}
#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid "A remote-controlled car.  Fun for young and old alike."
msgstr "一辆遥控车，老少皆宜。"

#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid "RC car (on)"
msgid_plural "RC cars (on)"
msgstr[0] "遥控车（开）"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'RC car (on)', 'str_pl': 'RC cars (on)'}
#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid ""
"This remote-controlled car is on, and draining its batteries just like a "
"real electric car!  Use a remote control to drive it around."
msgstr "这辆遥控车已经开启，正跟正儿八经的电动车一样吃着电池！使用无线控制器来驾驶它。"

#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid "radio activation mod"
msgid_plural "radio activation mods"
msgstr[0] "无线电启动器"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'radio activation mod'}
#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid ""
"This small piece of electronics can be attached to certain items and "
"activate them after receiving a radio signal."
msgstr "这件小型电子元件可以被附加到某些物品上，将在接受到一个无线电信号后开启。"

#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid "radio (off)"
msgid_plural "radios (off)"
msgstr[0] "收音机（关）"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'radio (off)', 'str_pl': 'radios (off)'}
#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid ""
"This is a portable radio.  Using this radio turns it on.  It will pick up "
"any nearby signals being broadcast and play them audibly."
msgstr "无线电，能够接受信号，并转化为声波。据说要是对准了信号塔，声音会格外响亮。"

#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid "radio (on)"
msgid_plural "radios (on)"
msgstr[0] "收音机（开）"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'radio (on)', 'str_pl': 'radios (on)'}
#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid ""
"This portable radio is turned on, and continually draining its batteries.  "
"It is playing the broadcast being sent from any nearby radio towers."
msgstr "这台无线电设备已经被启动，不停消耗着电池的同时不断向你播送着附近电台传出的资讯。"

#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid "two-way radio"
msgid_plural "two-way radios"
msgstr[0] "双向无线电"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'two-way radio'}
#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid ""
"This is a radio with a transmitting unit.  You could use it to contact "
"someone who also has one.  Unfortunately no one seems to use those nowadays…"
msgstr "这是一个有数据传输模块的无线电手台，你可以用它和另一个有这个手台的人联系。只是，在这个年头，好像没有人用这个了……"

#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid "remote vehicle controller"
msgid_plural "remote vehicle controllers"
msgstr[0] "载具远程遥控器"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'remote vehicle controller'}
#: data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid ""
"A remote controller for real cars.  Can turn onboard devices on and off.  "
"Some cars can be driven remotely."
msgstr "一个真车的遥控器。可以打开和关闭机载设备。有些汽车还可以远程驾驶。"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'birchbark funnel'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid "You place the birchbark funnel, waiting to collect rain."
msgstr "你安置了桦皮集雨器，等待收集雨水。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'birchbark funnel'}
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid ""
"This is a small birchbark funnel.  Place it above an outdoor container to "
"collect rainwater."
msgstr "这是一个小型桦树集雨器。放置在室外的容器上来收集雨水。"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'funnel'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid "You place the funnel, waiting to collect rain."
msgstr "你安置了集雨器，等待收集雨水。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'funnel'}
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid ""
"This is a funnel used to collect rainwater.  Use it outside and place a "
"container beneath it to collect water when it rains."
msgstr "一个用来收集雨水的漏斗状装置。在户外激活该物品把它放在地上，然后在它下面放一个容器就可以收集雨水了。"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'leather funnel'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid "You place the leather funnel, waiting to collect rain."
msgstr "你安置了皮革集雨器，等待收集雨水。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'leather funnel'}
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid ""
"This is a small, leather funnel used to collect rainwater.  Use it outside "
"and place a container beneath it to collect water when it rains."
msgstr "一个用来收集雨水的小型皮革漏斗状装置。在户外激活该物品把它放在地上，然后在它下面放一个容器就可以收集雨水了。"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'makeshift funnel'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid "You place the makeshift funnel, waiting to collect rain."
msgstr "你放置了简易集雨器，万事俱备，只待下雨了。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'makeshift funnel'}
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid ""
"This is a small, makeshift funnel used to collect rainwater.  Use it outside"
" and place a container beneath it to collect water when it rains."
msgstr "一个用来收集雨水的小型手工简易漏斗状装置。在户外激活该物品把它放在地上，然后在它下面放一个容器就可以收集雨水了。"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'metal funnel'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid "You place the metal funnel, waiting to collect rain."
msgstr "你安置了金属集雨器，等待收集雨水。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'metal funnel'}
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid ""
"This is a large metal funnel used to collect rainwater.  Less portable than "
"plastic funnels, but collects more water.  Use it outside and place a "
"container beneath it to collect water when it rains."
msgstr ""
"一个用来收集雨水的大型金属漏斗状装置。相较于塑料版更难移动，但能收集更多水。在户外激活该物品把它放在地上，然后在它下面放一个容器就可以收集雨水了。"

#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "tarp raincatcher"
msgid_plural "tarp raincatchers"
msgstr[0] "防水帆布集雨器"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'tarp raincatcher'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid "You set up the raincatcher, waiting to collect water."
msgstr "你设置了防水帆布集雨器，等待收集水。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'tarp raincatcher'}
#: data/json/items/tool/raincatchers.json
msgid ""
"Some sticks and string with a tarp to set up an improvised raincatcher."
msgstr "用一些棍子、绳子和一块防水布来搭建一个简易的雨水收集器。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "barometer"
msgid_plural "barometers"
msgstr[0] "气压计"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'barometer'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "A plastic barometer that can read the atmospheric pressure."
msgstr "一个塑料气压计，可以让你知道当前气压。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "goo canister"
msgid_plural "goo canisters"
msgstr[0] "粘液罐"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'goo canister'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"There is a label on this canister: \"Warning: contains highly toxic and "
"corrosive materials.  Contents may be sentient.  Open at your own risk.\" "
"You think you can feel something moving inside it."
msgstr "罐子上贴着个标签：\"警告：内含剧毒及极强腐蚀性物质！该物质具有自主意识！开启后果自负！\"你感觉到里面有什么东西在动。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "chemistry set"
msgid_plural "chemistry sets"
msgstr[0] "化学用品包"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'chemistry set'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a chemistry set stored in a box.  The contents include glass "
"containers, hoses, metal wire, a hotplate, and safety glasses.  It might be "
"used to craft some chemistry projects if you're so inclined."
msgstr ""
"这是一整套装在盒子里的化学实验装置，包括一些玻璃器皿、软管、金属导线、加热板以及护目镜。如果你需要的话，它可用来制造化学用品。\n"
"\"用于制造纯度高达99.1%的淡蓝色结晶。\""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "basic chemistry set"
msgid_plural "basic chemistry sets"
msgstr[0] "基础化学用品包"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'basic chemistry set'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a basic chemistry set which includes glass containers, hoses and "
"safety glasses.  It might be used to craft some chemistry projects if you're"
" so inclined, but you'll need a source of heat."
msgstr "这是一整套基本的化学实验装置，包括一些玻璃器皿、软管以及护目镜。如果你需要的话，它可用来制造化学用品。这件物品需要热源。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "electrolysis kit"
msgid_plural "electrolysis kits"
msgstr[0] "电解工具箱"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'electrolysis kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A set of wiring and electrodes for applying a direct current, usually to a "
"liquid.  Useful for crafting.  Load with a storage battery or 12V vehicle "
"battery to use."
msgstr "一整套能够进行直流电电解的线缆和电极设备，通常使用在液体上。可用于制造物品。需要安装一个蓄电池或者12V的载具电池配合使用。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "hydrogen tank"
msgid_plural "hydrogen tanks"
msgstr[0] "氢气罐"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'hydrogen tank'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a tank of compressed hydrogen gas.  If you need to make water from "
"scratch, or lift a zeppelin, it could come in handy."
msgstr "这是一个压缩氢气罐。如果你需要从零开始制造水，或者让一架齐柏林飞艇升空，它可能会派上用场。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "hygrometer"
msgid_plural "hygrometers"
msgstr[0] "湿度计"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'hygrometer'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "A plastic hygrometer that can read the relative humidity in the air."
msgstr "一个塑料湿度计，可以让你知道当前相对湿度。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "nitrogen tank"
msgid_plural "nitrogen tanks"
msgstr[0] "氮气罐"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'nitrogen tank'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a tank of compressed nitrogen gas.  Nitrogen is useful for its lack "
"of reactivity.  Don't try to breathe it."
msgstr ""
"这是一个压缩氮气罐。氮气化学性质稳定，非常有用。\n"
"\"警告：禁止口鼻接触。\""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "oxygen cylinder"
msgid_plural "oxygen cylinders"
msgstr[0] "氧气罐"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'oxygen cylinder'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A large steel cylinder used for storing pressurized gas.  It is marked with "
"a faded, but legible O2 symbol."
msgstr "一个用于储存高压气体的大型钢罐。上面有着一个依稀可见的 O2 标记。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "carbon dioxide tank"
msgid_plural "carbon dioxide tanks"
msgstr[0] "二氧化碳罐"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'carbon dioxide tank'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "This is a tank of compressed carbon dioxide gas."
msgstr "这是一个压缩二氧化碳气体的罐子。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "platinum grille"
msgid_plural "platinum grilles"
msgstr[0] "铂金格栅"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'platinum grille'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a metal grille with a layer of platinum plating, suitable for use as"
" a catalyst for some chemical reactions."
msgstr "一个带有一层铂金镀层的金属格栅，可在某些化学反应中当作催化剂使用。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "portal generator"
msgid_plural "portal generators"
msgstr[0] "传送门发生器"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'portal generator'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a rare, bizarre, and arcane device of an otherworldly nature.  It's "
"giving you a headache just looking at it.  It is covered in alien markings."
msgstr "一个罕见、奇异、不可思议的来自异界的装置。光是盯着它看上一会就会让你头疼。上面覆盖了各种奇特的陌生符号。"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'teleport pad'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "You place the telepad."
msgstr "你放置了触发板。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'teleport pad'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a kit for a teleporter trap consisting of a teleporter and a solar "
"cell that is triggered when stepped upon."
msgstr "这是一个由传送器和太阳能电池组成的传送陷阱，踩上去会触发它。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "teleporter"
msgid_plural "teleporters"
msgstr[0] "单人传送器"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'teleporter'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is an experimental device that will teleport you a short distance when "
"activated."
msgstr "这是一个神秘的装置，激活后能让你传送一小段距离。至于会不会传到怪物堆里，那就听天由命了。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "Doppler Radar Turbo 2000"
msgid_plural "Doppler Radar Turbo 2000s"
msgstr[0] "涡轮2000型全息多普勒气象分析仪"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'Doppler Radar Turbo 2000'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A briefcase with built-in laptop that looks like it's from the 80s.  Its "
"vintage monochrome monitor displays a plethora of meteorological data.  No "
"sign of the FLDSMDFR, however."
msgstr ""
"一个公文箱，内嵌一台看起来像是80年代老货的笔记本电脑。它古董的单色显示器上显示着大量的气象数据。不过貌似它没法帮你找到什么超级食物制造机。（注：出自电影《美食从天降》）"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "basic laboratory analysis kit"
msgid_plural "basic laboratory analysis kits"
msgstr[0] "基础实验室分析工具包"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'basic laboratory analysis kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This hefty kit contains some basic things you should probably not try to do "
"precise chemistry without: namely, a small balance scale, a "
"spectrophotometer, a melting point apparatus, a pH meter, and a set of paper"
" for thin layer chromatography.  This makes it a lot easier to feel "
"confident that the chemical you've made is what you think you've made."
msgstr ""
"这个庞大的试剂盒包含了一些基本测量工具，是你在进行任何精确化学操作时不可或缺的工具：包含一个小天平，一个分光度计，一个熔点仪，一个pH计，和一套色谱层析试纸。这让你更确信自己制造出来的化学品的成分是你所想要的成分。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "small weight scale"
msgid_plural "small weight scales"
msgstr[0] "小型天平"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'small weight scale'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a simple scale that uses a set of steel weights on sliding bars to "
"measure a sample's mass quite accurately."
msgstr "一个小型平衡称，使用一套钢制砝码以及滑条，能够精确测量样品的质量。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "spectrophotometer"
msgid_plural "spectrophotometers"
msgstr[0] "分光度计"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'spectrophotometer'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This ubiquitous analytical chemistry tool measures the light absorption of a"
" liquid sample in a special tube called a cuvette."
msgstr "一个十分常见的分析化学工具，用于测量液体样品在一种被称作比色皿的特殊试管中吸光率。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "pH meter"
msgid_plural "pH meters"
msgstr[0] "PH计"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pH meter'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is basically a pair of glass probes on a voltmeter.  By putting one "
"probe into a calibration solution (conveniently included) and the other in a"
" substance, you can calculate the acidity."
msgstr "一个带着一对玻璃探针的电压表。通过将探针分别放入标准溶液（仪器已配套）和待测物质中，你可以测量酸碱度。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "voltmeter"
msgid_plural "voltmeters"
msgstr[0] "电压表"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'voltmeter'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This device has two probes that let you measure the electrical potential "
"between two points.  Activate to check the status of any local grid "
"connections or battery charge in your surroundings, as well as make "
"modifications to grid connections"
msgstr "这个设备有两个探针，让您可以测量两个点之间的电位。激活它可以检查周围任何本地电网连接或电池充电的状态，并且可以对电网连接进行修改。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "melting point apparatus"
msgid_plural "units of melting point apparatus"
msgstr[0] "熔点仪"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'melting point apparatus', 'str_pl': 'units of
#. melting point apparatus'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is basically a hot plate, with a metal housing attached.  The metal "
"housing has a magnification viewport and a slot into which a capillary tube "
"containing a crystallized sample is inserted.  The device lets you precisely"
" measure the melting point of a crystal, a property very useful in "
"identifying what it is and how pure it is."
msgstr ""
"一个电炉，外带一个金属外壳。金属外壳上有个带放大镜的观察口，以及一个能插入装有结晶样品的细试管的插槽。这个仪器可以让你精确测量晶体的熔点，可用于鉴定样品的纯度。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "vortex device"
msgid_plural "vortex devices"
msgstr[0] "涡旋仪"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'vortex device'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a small, hefty, boring looking machine.  Its weighted trapezoidal "
"frame has a single on-off switch and a speed dial, and on top of it sits a "
"rubber receptacle.  Pressing a test tube into the receptacle would, with "
"power, rapidly shake and mix the contents of the test tube.  It's "
"surprisingly fun to use."
msgstr ""
"这是一台小巧、笨重、看起来很无聊的机器。它的加重梯形框架上有一个独立开关和一个快速拨号盘，顶部有一个橡胶容器。将试管压入容器中，通电后会迅速摇晃并混合试管中的内容物。使用起来出人意料的有趣。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "light detector"
msgid_plural "light detectors"
msgstr[0] "检光器"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'light detector'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a photodiode on a chip, designed to convert incoming light to "
"electrical energy for quantification."
msgstr "一个安装在芯片上的光电二极管，可以用来将入射光转换成电能并进行测量。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "glass prism"
msgid_plural "glass prisms"
msgstr[0] "玻璃棱镜"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'glass prism'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a high quality crystal glass prism for separating and redirecting "
"light."
msgstr "一个质量很好的水晶玻璃棱镜，用于分离并改变不同频率光的光路。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "small glass tube"
msgid_plural "small glass tubes"
msgstr[0] "小型玻璃试管"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'small glass tube'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a small glass tube.  What more could you possibly want to know about"
" it?"
msgstr "一根小型玻璃管。你还想知道些什么？"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "microscope"
msgid_plural "microscopes"
msgstr[0] "显微镜"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'microscope'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"A classic tool for the ages!  This hefty, durable piece of lab equipment "
"makes small things look bigger.  Without electricity the light doesn't work,"
" but the rest of it is surprisingly functional.  Unfortunately it's not "
"useful for very much at the moment."
msgstr ""
"一个经典的工具！这件笨重耐用的实验室设备能让你更清晰地看到小东西。由于没有电，它的灯泡不能工作，但其余的功能却非常完好。不幸的是，事到如今它也没有太多用处了。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "dissecting microscope"
msgid_plural "dissecting microscopes"
msgstr[0] "解剖显微镜"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'dissecting microscope'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This microscope has less magnification than a standard one.  It's also "
"stereoscopic and produces a neat 3d image of the surface.  It was typically "
"used for doing dissections and other fine detail work on small creatures.  "
"It still works pretty well with an added light source, but what would you do"
" with it?"
msgstr ""
"这台显微镜的放大倍数比标准显微镜小。它也有立体视觉功能，可以生成表面清晰的三维图像。它通常用于对小生物进行解剖或其他精细的工作，添加附加光源后非常好用，但你会如何使用它？"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "separation funnel"
msgid_plural "separation funnels"
msgstr[0] "分液漏斗"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'separation funnel'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This thing doesn't look much like a funnel.  It's a teardrop shaped piece of"
" glass with a stopper at the wide end and a valve at the other.  It can be "
"used to wash one liquid with another, like water and an oil, and then draw "
"off whichever of the two liquids contains a higher amount of whatever "
"compound you're trying to isolate.  With a high level of skill it can also "
"be used to make juvenile farting noises."
msgstr ""
"这东西看起来不像漏斗，更像一块泪珠状的玻璃，宽端有一个塞子，另一端有一个阀门。它可以用来分离一种液体和另一种液体，如水和油，然后抽出两种液体中你要离析的化合物。如果你的技术水平够高，它也可以用来制造幼稚的放屁声。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "rotary evaporator"
msgid_plural "rotary evaporators"
msgstr[0] "旋转蒸发仪"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'rotary evaporator'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"Just looking at this thing makes you feel like a proper mad scientist.  It's"
" a series of glass tubes and round flasks, connected to a central motor and "
"a heating element.  The heating element warms one flask, kept rotating by "
"the motor, evaporating the contents.  The vapour is then condensed in the "
"tubes and collected in another flask, in case you wanted to save it for "
"later."
msgstr ""
"只要看看这东西，你就会觉得自己是个真正的疯狂科学家。一系列玻璃管和圆烧瓶连接到一个中央电机和一个加热器上。加热器加热一个烧瓶，电机使它保持转动，令内容物蒸发。然后，蒸汽在试管中冷凝，并收集到另一个烧瓶中，以备以后使用。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "fractional distillation apparatus"
msgid_plural "fractional distillation apparati"
msgstr[0] "分馏装置"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'fractional distillation apparatus', 'str_pl':
#. 'fractional distillation apparati'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"One of the classic pieces of mad science glassware, this is basically a "
"small volume still that passes the vapour through a fractional distillation "
"column and then condenses the distillate in a cooled collection column.  A "
"grad student or a robot (is there really any difference?) collects the "
"distillate in fractions so that specific contents can be analyzed.  Going a "
"few milliliters at a time, it would not be very effective to try to distill "
"whiskey in this thing."
msgstr ""
"这是一件经典的疯狂科学玻璃器皿，基本上是一个小体积的蒸馏器，蒸馏物的蒸汽通过分馏塔，然后在一个冷却的收集塔中冷凝。研究生或机器人（真的有什么区别吗？）将蒸馏液收集起来，以便分析具体的成分。如果你用它来蒸馏威士忌，每次大概只能得到几毫升。"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "electrophoresis tray"
msgid_plural "electrophoresis trays"
msgstr[0] "电泳托盘"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'electrophoresis tray'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a set of plastic trays, electrodes, and a power supply designed to "
"create an electric voltage gradient through a liquid solution containing a "
"solid gel.  Stuff like proteins and DNA would then get separated on the gel "
"according to electrical charge and size.  Pretty useless now, for anything "
"but salvage."
msgstr ""
"这是一组塑料托盘、电极和电源，用于通过含有固体凝胶的液体溶液产生电压梯度。然后，像蛋白质和DNA之类的物质会根据电荷和大小在凝胶上分离。\n"
"\"现在这只是可回收垃圾。\""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "microcentrifuge"
msgid_plural "microcentrifuges"
msgstr[0] "微型离心机"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'microcentrifuge'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"This is a smaller, benchtop version of the larger furniture-sized "
"centrifuge.  Don't be fooled by its portable scale; it's still a very "
"powerful piece of equipment that can spin stuff really quickly.  It's not a "
"toy!"
msgstr "这是一个较小版本的，台式的大型家具大小的离心机。别被它的便携式天平欺骗了，它仍然是一个非常强大的设备，可以快速旋转东西。这不是玩具！"

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "3D printer"
msgid_plural "3D printers"
msgstr[0] "3D打印机"

#. ~ Description for {'str': '3D printer'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"Although it's not nearly as fancy as the experimental nanofabricators, this "
"civilian-grade 3D printer can produce almost any item out of plastic, "
"polymer, or carbon fiber…  so long as you can program it.  It's also useful "
"for repairing items made out of plastic or carbon fiber."
msgstr ""
"虽然这款民用级3D打印机不像纳米制造实验机那样花哨，但它几乎可以用塑料、聚合物或碳纤维制造任何物品......只要你会编程。它也可用于修复塑料或碳纤维制品。\n"
"\"我会编程，但我不会3D建模啊喂。\""

#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "advanced 3D printer"
msgid_plural "advanced 3D printers"
msgstr[0] "高级3D打印机"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'advanced 3D printer'}
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid ""
"Recent advances in 3D printing technology have resulted in the ability to "
"quickly and cheaply 3D print metals and alloys.  Such 3D printers are highly"
" expensive, but sought out by collectors and preppers alike.  In addition to"
" crafting, it can be used to repair polymer and metal items alike, or "
"permeate fabric items with carbon fiber for added protection."
msgstr ""
"3D打印技术的最新进展使得人们能够快速、廉价地3D打印金属和合金。 这种3D打印机价格昂贵，但却受到收藏家和准备者的青睐。除了制造外，它还可用于修复聚合物和金属制品，或为织物注入碳纤维以提供额外防护。\n"
"\"连老婆都能打印出来！\""

#: data/json/items/tool/shelters.json
msgid "damaged shelter kit"
msgid_plural "damaged shelter kits"
msgstr[0] "简易棚屋（损坏）"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'damaged shelter kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/shelters.json
msgid ""
"This is a small shelter, made of sticks and skins.  Use it to place.  This "
"shelter has been damaged, and needs repairs."
msgstr "用毛皮和木棍组合成的小帐篷，可以把它架设在地面上。顺便提醒一下，它似乎受损了，最好修一修。激活它来放置。"

#: data/json/items/tool/shelters.json
msgid "large tent"
msgid_plural "large tents"
msgstr[0] "大帐篷"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'large tent'}
#: data/json/items/tool/shelters.json
msgid ""
"This is a family sized tent.  It provides a large amount of space, but is "
"very bulky."
msgstr "这是一只供全家出行使用的帐篷，可以提供大量的空间，但十分笨重。"

#: data/json/items/tool/shelters.json
msgid "shelter kit"
msgid_plural "shelter kits"
msgstr[0] "简易棚屋"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'shelter kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/shelters.json
msgid "This is a small shelter, made of sticks and skins.  Use it to place."
msgstr "用毛皮和木棍组合成的小帐篷，可以把它架设在地面上。"

#: data/json/items/tool/shelters.json
msgid "tent"
msgid_plural "tents"
msgstr[0] "帐篷"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'tent'}
#: data/json/items/tool/shelters.json
msgid ""
"This is a small personal tent, it's just big enough to fit you comfortably."
msgstr "一顶小帐篷，足够一个人舒舒服服地钻进去睡大觉。"

#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid "boxmod vape"
msgid_plural "boxmod vapes"
msgstr[0] "盒式电子烟"

#. ~ Use action activation_message for {'str': 'boxmod vape'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid "You take a puff from your boxmod vape."
msgstr "你吸了一口盒式电子烟。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'boxmod vape'}
#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid ""
"An advanced version of the electronic cigarette.  A less harmful way to get "
"your nicotine fix than regular cigarettes, but still addictive.  It needs "
"batteries and nicotine liquid to function.  The side has a display showing "
"the battery and amount of nicotine liquid left.  Additionally, it allows you"
" to play simple games on it."
msgstr ""
"电子香烟的高级版本。和普通香烟比起来摄取尼古丁的方式要柔和得多，不过照样会让你上瘾。需要电池和尼古丁浓缩液来运作。侧面有一个显示屏，显示剩余电量和尼古丁液量。此外，还可以玩简单的小游戏。"

#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid "disposable vape"
msgid_plural "disposable vapes"
msgstr[0] "一次性电子烟"

#. ~ Use action activation_message for disposable vape.
#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid "You take a puff from your disposable vape."
msgstr "你吸了一口一次性电子烟。"

#. ~ Description for disposable vape
#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid ""
"This battery-operated device vaporizes a liquid that contains flavorings and"
" nicotine.  A less harmful alternative to traditional cigarettes, but it's "
"still addictive.  It can't be reused once it's empty.  The side has a "
"display showing the battery and amount of nicotine liquid left."
msgstr ""
"这个电池驱动的装置将尼古丁和调味剂的混合液蒸腾起来，虽然比燃烧型的卷烟伤害低一点，但是同样上瘾。它是一次性使用的，耗尽后无法复装。侧面有显示屏，显示电量和剩余尼古丁液量。"

#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid "crack pipe"
msgid_plural "crack pipes"
msgstr[0] "烟管"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'crack pipe'}
#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid ""
"This is a fine glass tube with a bulb with a bowl on one end.  It's used to "
"partake of certain illicit substances."
msgstr "一个细玻璃管，底部可以点火。用来享用某些，你懂的，非法的违禁物质。"

#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid "glass pipe"
msgid_plural "glass pipes"
msgstr[0] "玻璃烟管"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'glass pipe'}
#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid ""
"This is a hand-blown glass pipe.  It's of the type most commonly used to "
"smoke recreational substances."
msgstr "一个手工吹制而成的玻璃管，经常被用来吸食迷幻类植物制品。"

#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid "glass bong"
msgid_plural "glass bongs"
msgstr[0] "玻璃水烟壶"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'glass bong'}
#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid ""
"This is a hand-blown glass beaker bong.  Easy to clean, hard to tip over, "
"and functional even after society collapses."
msgstr "这是一个手工吹制的玻璃烧杯式水烟壶。易于清洁，不易倾倒，即使社会崩坏也依然能用。"

#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid "tobacco pipe"
msgid_plural "tobacco pipes"
msgstr[0] "烟斗"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'tobacco pipe'}
#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid ""
"This is a hand-carved wooden smoking pipe.  It's designed to facilitate "
"consumption of fire cured tobacco leaves."
msgstr "一个手工雕刻而成的烟斗，可以用来吸食烟叶。"

#. ~ Use action activation_message for {'str': 'dab pen'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid "You hit your dab pen. Sooooo smooth..."
msgstr "你吸了一口电子吸油笔。*咳咳*好货色！"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'dab pen'}
#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid ""
"This is a dab pen for vaporizing cannabis.  Now all you need is 'thc "
"distillate' and you're ready to rock and roll."
msgstr "这是一个用于蒸发大麻的电子吸油笔。你只需要再准备好\"THC蒸馏物\"，就可以开始嗨起来了。"

#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid "disposable dab pen"
msgid_plural "disposable dab pens"
msgstr[0] "一次性电子吸油笔"

#. ~ Use action activation_message for {'str': 'disposable dab pen'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid "You hit your disposable dab pen. Sooooo smooth..."
msgstr "你吸了一口一次性电子吸油笔。*咳咳*好货色！"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'disposable dab pen'}
#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid ""
"This is a disposable dab pen for vaporizing cannabis.  This one is already "
"filled with distillate for your convenience, but can't be recharged."
msgstr "这是一个一次性使用的电子吸油笔，专用于蒸发大麻。里面已经预装了蒸馏物，使用方便，但无法充电或重复使用。"

#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid "nectar collector"
msgid_plural "nectar collectors"
msgstr[0] "蜜采器"

#. ~ Use action activation_message for {'str': 'nectar collector'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid "You heat the nectar collector and hit it. Sooooo smooth..."
msgstr "你加热蜜采器并吸了一口。*咳咳*好货色！"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'nectar collector'}
#: data/json/items/tool/smoking.json
msgid ""
"This is a metal and wooden nectar collector.  The top cover can be attached "
"and detached magnetically.  The wood has engravings depicting bees, honey, "
"and flowers.  You need 'thc wax' to use this item."
msgstr "这是一款由金属和木材制成的蜜采器。顶部盖子可以通过磁力吸附和拆卸。木制部分雕刻着蜜蜂、蜂蜜和花朵的图案。使用此物品需要 \"THC 蜡\"。"

#: data/json/items/tool/stationary.json
msgid "stapler"
msgid_plural "staplers"
msgstr[0] "订书机"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'stapler'}
#: data/json/items/tool/stationary.json
msgid "A stapler for fastening sheets of paper together."
msgstr "一种将纸张固定在一起的订书机。"

#: data/json/items/tool/stationary.json
msgid "pen"
msgid_plural "pens"
msgstr[0] "圆珠笔"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pen'}
#: data/json/items/tool/stationary.json
msgid "A plastic ball point pen."
msgstr "一根塑料圆珠笔。"

#: data/json/items/tool/stationary.json
msgid "pair of scissors"
msgid_plural "pairs of scissors"
msgstr[0] "剪刀"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pair of scissors', 'str_pl': 'pairs of
#. scissors'}
#: data/json/items/tool/stationary.json
msgid ""
"These are a long pair of heavy-duty scissors.  Use scissors to cut items "
"made from cotton (like clothing) into rags."
msgstr "一把耐用的工艺长剪刀。使用它可以衣物等棉制物品剪割成布条，或有其它用途。"

#: data/json/items/tool/stationary.json
msgid "paper"
msgid_plural "papers"
msgstr[0] "纸"

#. ~ Description for paper
#: data/json/items/tool/stationary.json
msgid "A piece of paper.  Can be used for fires."
msgstr "一张纸，可以用来生火。"

#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "bone sewing awl"
msgid_plural "bone sewing awls"
msgstr[0] "骨制缝纫锥"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bone sewing awl'}
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"This is a crude sharpened bone awl; those were used for leatherworking "
"before metal was discovered.  It can also serve as an improvised stabbing "
"weapon, but will break quickly."
msgstr "一个经过粗糙打磨成型的骨锥；早在人类发现金属之前就被用于制造皮革物品了。它也能够当作一把简易的刺击武器，但会很快损坏。"

#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "steel sewing awl"
msgid_plural "steel sewing awls"
msgstr[0] "钢制缝纫锥"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'steel sewing awl'}
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"This is a steel awl with a wooden grip, usually used for leatherworking.  It"
" can also serve as an improvised stabbing weapon, but will break quickly."
msgstr "一个带着木头手柄的钢锥，能够用于制造皮革物品。它也能够当作一把简易的刺击武器，但会很快损坏。"

#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "knitting needles"
msgid_plural "pairs of knitting needles"
msgstr[0] "棒针"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'knitting needles', 'str_pl': 'pairs of knitting
#. needles'}
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A pair of stout wooden needles with round ends used to turn thread and yarn "
"into cloth."
msgstr "一组结实的圆头木针，用来将线织成布。"

#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "bone needle"
msgid_plural "bone needles"
msgstr[0] "骨针"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bone needle'}
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"This is sharp needle made from a bone.  It would be useful for making rough "
"clothing and items.  Its low quality makes it rather unsuitable for anything"
" requiring speed or precision."
msgstr "一根由骨头制成的锐利针头。可用来制造粗糙的简易服装和物品。它低劣的品质使它不适合用来制造任何需要精度或速度的物品。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'curved needle'}
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A curved sharp needle made of steel.  Its rounded shape allows it to make "
"stitches that only pierce one side of the material.  While unsuitable for "
"most tailoring projects, it's a necessity for stitching neoprene."
msgstr "一种钢制的弯曲的尖针。它的圆形的形状可以使它只穿透的材料的一侧。虽然不适合大多数的裁缝工作，但这是拼接氯丁橡胶的必需品。"

#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "wooden needle"
msgid_plural "wooden needles"
msgstr[0] "木针"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wooden needle'}
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"This is a wooden needle whittled down to a sharp point.  It has a narrow "
"hole carved into the head for threading.  Its low quality makes it rather "
"unsuitable for anything requiring speed or precision, or involving tougher "
"materials like Kevlar."
msgstr "一根削尖的木针，上面有个刻出来的穿线孔。它低劣的品质使它不适合用来制造任何需要精度或速度的物品，或者用于类似于凯夫拉的坚硬材质上。"

#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
#: data/mods/MagicalNights/items/tools.json
msgid "sewing kit"
msgid_plural "sewing kits"
msgstr[0] "缝纫工具箱"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'sewing kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"This is a plastic kit with a variety of needles, some plastic spools for "
"thread, and a few other useful textile tools.  Use a sewing kit on an "
"article of clothing to attempt to repair or reinforce that clothing.  This "
"uses your tailoring skill, and can also sew pockets or warmer liner into "
"your gear, or resize it for mutant wearers."
msgstr ""
"一个装有各种针线和纹理工具的小缝纫盒。使用缝纫工具可以修复或者加固各类服饰，这需要用到你的缝纫技能，也可以为你的装备缝上口袋或保暖内衬，或为变种人穿着者调整尺寸。"

#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "tailoring pattern set"
msgid_plural "tailoring pattern sets"
msgstr[0] "缝纫用模板"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'tailoring pattern set'}
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"This is a large set of tailoring patterns made from paper.  They're useful "
"for making any kind of cloth or leather items from scratch, but are "
"necessary for more advanced projects."
msgstr "这是一大套纸制的缝纫用模板，可以用来从头制造布料或者皮革衣物，在更复杂的裁缝工作中更是必不可少。"

#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
#: data/mods/MagicalNights/items/tools.json
msgid "tailor's kit"
msgid_plural "tailor's kits"
msgstr[0] "裁缝助手"

#. ~ Description for {'str': "tailor's kit"}
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"This is a high quality kit consisting of a variety of needles, some plastic "
"spools for thread, some small scissors, and an awl.  Using your tailoring "
"skill, this kit can customize your clothing and armor, whether up-armoring "
"them or altering some items to fit mutant wearers."
msgstr ""
"一个装着各种针、几卷线，几把小剪刀，以及一把锥子的高品质缝纫工具箱。通过您的裁缝技能，这个工具包可以定制您的服装和盔甲，无论是加强它们的防御力还是修改一些项目以适应突变生物的穿戴。"

#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "bathroom scale"
msgid_plural "bathroom scales"
msgstr[0] "体重秤"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bathroom scale'}
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "This is a small bathroom scale, meant to weigh a person while naked."
msgstr "这是一个小型的浴室秤，用来称一个人裸体时的体重。"

#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "scrub brush"
msgid_plural "scrub brushes"
msgstr[0] "刷子"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'scrub brush', 'str_pl': 'scrub brushes'}
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "This is a simple scrub brush."
msgstr "这是一个简单的刷子。"

#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json data/mods/change_hairstyle/item.json
msgid "electric hair trimmer"
msgid_plural "electric hair trimmers"
msgstr[0] "电动理发剪"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'electric hair trimmer'}
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"This is a pocket-sized electric trimmer made for cutting hair.  You can use "
"it to cut your hair if it's supplied with batteries.  It requires 10 "
"batteries per use."
msgstr "一个小巧的电动理发剪。如果你有电池，你可以用它剪头发。每次使用需要10单位的电池。"

#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "mop"
msgid_plural "mops"
msgstr[0] "拖把"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'mop'}
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"This is an unwieldy mop.  Good for cleaning up spills.  Use to mop up any "
"'mess' you may have made."
msgstr "笨重的拖把，清理泄漏的液体很不错。"

#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "collapsible mop"
msgid_plural "collapsible mops"
msgstr[0] "折叠拖把"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'collapsible mop'}
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"A long unwieldy mop with a collapsible handle for convenient transportation."
"  You may use it to clean up any 'mess' you have made."
msgstr "一款长柄而笨重的拖把，配有可折叠手柄，便于运输。你可以用它清理任何你制造的\"混乱\"。"

#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "razor blade"
msgid_plural "razor blades"
msgstr[0] "剃须刀片"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'razor blade'}
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"A double-edged razor blade.  Finicky to use on its own, but can be used as a"
" cutting tool in a pinch."
msgstr "一片双刃剃须刀片。单独使用时很难操作，但在紧急情况下可以作为切割工具使用。"

#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "shaving kit"
msgid_plural "shaving kits"
msgstr[0] "刮胡刀套装"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'shaving kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"This is a compact and lightweight shaving kit made for travelers.  You can "
"use it to shave if it's supplied with soap.  It requires 1 unit of soap per "
"use."
msgstr "一个为旅行者准备的紧凑、轻便的刮胡刀工具包。如果你有肥皂，你可以用它刮胡子。每次使用需要1单位的肥皂"

#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "sponge"
msgid_plural "sponges"
msgstr[0] "海绵"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'sponge'}
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"A sponge is a tool or cleaning aid made of soft, porous material.  Typically"
" used for cleaning impervious surfaces, it can also be used for sanding wood"
" when dried."
msgstr "海绵由多孔的软材料制成，可以拿来做清洁。通常用于清洁不透水的表面，在干燥状态下也可以用来打磨木材。"

#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json data/mods/change_hairstyle/item.json
msgid "makeshift haircut kit"
msgid_plural "makeshift haircut kits"
msgstr[0] "简易理发剪"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'makeshift haircut kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "This is a kit with tools for cutting hair."
msgstr "这是一套理发工具。"

#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "makeshift shaving kit"
msgid_plural "makeshift shaving kits"
msgstr[0] "简易剃须刀套装"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'makeshift shaving kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"This is a makeshift shaving kit.  You can use it to shave if it's supplied "
"with soap.  It requires 1 unit of soap per use."
msgstr "一把简易剃须刀。如果你有肥皂，你可以用它刮胡子。每次使用需要1单位的肥皂。"

#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "washboard"
msgid_plural "washboards"
msgstr[0] "洗衣板"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'washboard'}
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"This is a wooden washboard.  You can use it to wash filthy clothing if it's "
"supplied with cleansing agent."
msgstr "一块木制的洗衣板。如果你有肥皂，你可以用它洗脏衣服。每次使用需要消耗清洗剂。"

#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "washing kit"
msgid_plural "washing kits"
msgstr[0] "洗涤工具箱"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'washing kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"A combination kit of a washboard and a scrubbing tool.  Everything you need "
"to clean items after the apocalypse."
msgstr "洗衣板和洗刷工具组成的工具套装，这就是大灾变后洗涤所需的一切用具。"

#. ~ Use action bury_question for {'str': 'bear trap'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "Bury the beartrap?"
msgstr "确定埋下捕熊陷阱？"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'bear trap'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You set the beartrap."
msgstr "你设置了捕熊陷阱。"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'bear trap'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You bury the beartrap."
msgstr "你埋下了捕熊陷阱。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bear trap'}
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"This is a spring-loaded pair of steel jaws connected to a sensitive pressure"
" plate.  Use it to set it on the ground, creating a trap that will ensnare "
"and damage anything that steps on it.  If you are carrying a shovel, you "
"will have the option of burying it."
msgstr "一副装有压力板的铁爪。布置在地面上做成陷阱，可以保证每个失足踩上来的家伙喝上一壶。如果你随身带着铁锹，你还能把它埋在土里。"

#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "blade trap"
msgid_plural "blade traps"
msgstr[0] "刀刃陷阱"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'blade trap'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You set the blade trap %d squares away."
msgstr "你在%d格外设置了刀片陷阱。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'blade trap'}
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"This is a machete attached laterally to a motor, with a tripwire controlling"
" its throttle.  When the tripwire is pulled, the blade is swung around with "
"great force.  The trap forms a 3x3 area of effect."
msgstr "这是一把横向地连接在电动机上的砍刀，连接着一个开关。当按下开关，刀片就会像电风扇一样转起来，形成一个3x3面积的陷阱。"

#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "nailboard trap"
msgid_plural "nailboard traps"
msgstr[0] "钉板陷阱"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'nailboard trap'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You set the board trap on the %s, nails facing up."
msgstr "你成功在%s上安装了钉板陷阱 ，当然钉子朝上。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'nailboard trap'}
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"These are several pieces of wood nailed together, with some nails sticking "
"straight up.  If an unsuspecting victim steps on it, they'll get nails "
"through the foot."
msgstr "这是一块厚实的木板，其中一端上有几枚长长的钉子。你可以邀请你的敌人享受脚板的\"愉悦\"。"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'booby trap'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You set the booby trap up and activate the grenade."
msgstr "你设置了引信，然后激活了榴弹。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'booby trap'}
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"This is a crude explosive device triggered by a piece of string.  Use it to "
"set up and watch some poor bastard trigger it."
msgstr "由引线启动的简陋炸药。再也不用担心炸弹捻被人不小心踩灭的尴尬事情发生了。使用它来布置在地面上。"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'bubble wrap'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You set the bubble wrap on the ground, ready to be popped."
msgstr "你把泡泡卷铺在了地上，准备充气。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bubble wrap'}
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"This is a sheet of plastic covered with air-filled bubbles.  Use it to set "
"it on the ground, creating a trap that will warn you with noise when "
"something steps on it."
msgstr "这是一层又一层的泡沫塑料，如果有东西踩过它的话，会发出足够的响声以提醒在附近活动的你。"

#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "loose caltrops"
msgid_plural "loose caltrops"
msgstr[0] "铁蒺藜"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str_sp': 'loose caltrops'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You scatter the caltrops on the %s."
msgstr "你将铁蒺藜撒在%s上。"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'loose caltrops'}
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"These are small metal objects covered with many sharp points.  If an "
"unsuspecting victim steps on one, they'll get a spine through the foot."
msgstr "一些金属小刺猬，如果哪个倒霉蛋踩上去，就得担心破伤风的问题了。"

#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "loose glass caltrops"
msgid_plural "loose glass caltrops"
msgstr[0] "玻璃蒺藜"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str_sp': 'loose glass caltrops'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You scatter the glass caltrops on the %s."
msgstr "你将玻璃蒺藜撒在%s上。"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'loose glass caltrops'}
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"These are glass shards glued together to expose their sharp edges.  If an "
"unsuspecting victim steps on one, they'll get cut."
msgstr "这些玻璃碎片粘在一起，露出锋利的边缘。如果一个毫无戒心的受害者踩到一个，他们就会被收到伤害。"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'crossbow trap'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You set the crossbow trap."
msgstr "你设置了弩陷阱。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'crossbow trap'}
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"This is a simple tripwire, which is attached to the trigger of a loaded "
"crossbow.  When pulled, the crossbow fires.  Only a single round can be "
"used, after which the trap is disabled."
msgstr "一根轻巧的棉线轻柔地连在了弩的扳机之上，只要轻轻一拨，一支致命的短矢就会直奔目标而去，把它扎成巫毒娃娃。"

#. ~ Use action bury_question for {'str': 'land mine'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "Bury the land mine?"
msgstr "埋下地雷？"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'land mine'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You set the land mine."
msgstr "你设置了地雷。"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'land mine'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You bury the land mine."
msgstr "你埋下了地雷。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'land mine'}
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"This is a military anti-personnel mine that is triggered when stepped upon."
msgstr "这是一个已经埋设好的军用反人员地雷，一旦踩上就会爆炸。"

#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "double-barreled shotgun trap"
msgid_plural "double-barreled shotgun traps"
msgstr[0] "双管霰弹枪陷阱"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'double-barreled shotgun trap'}.
#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'shotgun trap'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You set the shotgun trap."
msgstr "你设置了霰弹枪陷阱。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'double-barreled shotgun trap'}
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"This is a simple tripwire is attached to the trigger of a loaded double-"
"barreled shotgun.  When pulled, the shotgun fires, discharging both barrels "
"into the target."
msgstr "这是一种简单的绊线，连接在装有子弹的双管猎枪扳机上。 扣动扳机后，霰弹枪就会开火，两支枪管都向目标射击。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'shotgun trap'}
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"This is a simple tripwire is attached to the trigger of a loaded single-"
"barreled shotgun.  When pulled, the shotgun fires."
msgstr "这是一个简单的绊线，连接在装有子弹的单管猎枪扳机上。 扣动扳机后，霰弹枪就会开火。"

#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "tripwire trap"
msgid_plural "tripwire traps"
msgstr[0] "绊索诱捕陷阱"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'tripwire trap'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You string up the tripwire."
msgstr "你安置了绊索。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'tripwire trap'}
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"This is some thin strong cable with some affixing tools on either end.  A "
"tripwire trap must be placed across a doorway or other thin passage.  Its "
"purpose is to trip up bypassers, causing them to stumble and possibly hurt "
"themselves slightly."
msgstr "绊索陷阱，只能设置在门口或是狭窄的走廊。它可以用来困住经过的对象，将对方绊倒的同时也可能造成轻微伤。"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'makeshift perimeter alarm'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You string up some cans on a tripwire."
msgstr "你在绊索上挂了一些罐头。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'makeshift perimeter alarm'}
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"This is a set of empty cans used as makeshift noisemakers, strung up across "
"a doorway or other thin passage.  It will make noise when activated to alert"
" you of intruders, but is otherwise harmless."
msgstr "这是一组空罐头，被用作临时制造的噪音制造器，被串在门口或其他狭窄通道上。当被触发时，会发出声音以警示您有入侵者，但除此之外是无害的。"

#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "glass shard trap"
msgid_plural "glass shard traps"
msgstr[0] "玻璃碎片陷阱"

#. ~ Use action done_message for {'str': 'glass shard trap'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"You carefully place the shards on the ground, ready to be cracked by "
"something passing by."
msgstr "你小心地将碎片放在地上，让它能被经过的东西压碎。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'glass shard trap'}
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"Same glass shard as before but you can activate it to place it on the "
"ground, it will make noise when stepped on."
msgstr "还是那些玻璃渣，但是你可以激活并放在地上，当有东西踩上去就会发出噪声。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "wood axe"
msgid_plural "wood axes"
msgstr[0] "伐木斧"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wood axe'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a large, two-handed wood axe.  It makes a good melee weapon, but is "
"a bit slow to recover between swings."
msgstr "巨大的双手斧。是个优秀的近战武器，至于速度比较慢，请不要在意这些细节。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "bronze axe"
msgid_plural "bronze axes"
msgstr[0] "青铜斧"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bronze axe'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a large, two-handed wood axe with a bronze axehead.  It makes a good"
" melee weapon, but is a bit slow to recover between swings."
msgstr "这是一把带有青铜斧头的大型双手伐木斧。它是一种出色的近战武器，但在挥动之间稍显缓慢恢复。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "chainsaw (off)"
msgid_plural "chainsaws (off)"
msgstr[0] "链锯（关）"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'chainsaw (off)', 'str_pl': 'chainsaws
#. (off)'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "You turn on the chainsaw."
msgstr "你启动了链锯。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'chainsaw (off)', 'str_pl': 'chainsaws (off)'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a lumbering tool moonlighting as weapon of opportunity.  If loaded "
"with gas, using this item will cause it to turn on, turning it into a very "
"powerful but unwieldy melee weapon."
msgstr "便利的伐木工具，偶尔也作为武器使用。装填汽油之后，激活它来开启。威力巨大，不过难以掌控。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "chainsaw (on)"
msgid_plural "chainsaws (on)"
msgstr[0] "链锯（开）"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'chainsaw (on)', 'str_pl': 'chainsaws (on)'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "You turn off the chainsaw."
msgstr "你关闭了链锯。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'chainsaw (on)', 'str_pl': 'chainsaws (on)'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "This chainsaw is on and making a lot of noise.  Use it to turn it off."
msgstr "链锯已经启动，发出可怕的噪声。激活它来关闭。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "circular saw (off)"
msgid_plural "circular saws (off)"
msgstr[0] "圆锯（关）"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'circular saw (off)', 'str_pl': 'circular saws
#. (off)'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "You turn on the circular saw."
msgstr "你启动了圆锯。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'circular saw (off)', 'str_pl': 'circular saws
#. (off)'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A lightweight handheld cordless circular saw.  Spins a circular blade fast "
"enough to cut wood, zombies, or in an emergency, pizza.  The blade, while "
"effective in combat, is hard to hit with due to its small size."
msgstr ""
"很轻的手持无线圆锯，能够用来切木头、丧尸或者……呃，如果你等不及了的话，也能切披萨。虽然刃片看起来能在战斗中起到很大作用，但体积太小，想用它打中敌人可不容易。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "circular saw (on)"
msgid_plural "circular saws (on)"
msgstr[0] "圆锯（开）"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'circular saw (on)', 'str_pl': 'circular saws
#. (on)'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "You turn off the circular saw."
msgstr "你关闭了圆锯。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'circular saw (on)', 'str_pl': 'circular saws
#. (on)'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A lightweight handheld cordless circular saw.  It is currently on and the "
"blade is spinning; use this item to turn it off."
msgstr "很轻的手持无线圆锯。它的刃片正高速旋转。激活它来关闭。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "copper axe"
msgid_plural "copper axes"
msgstr[0] "铜制斧头"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'copper axe'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a decent-sized chunk of worked copper affixed to a wooden shaft, to "
"make a crude yet effective axe."
msgstr "一个足够大的经过加工的铜块被安装在一个木制的手柄上，成了一把粗糙但有效的斧头。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "hatchet"
msgid_plural "hatchets"
msgstr[0] "短柄斧"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'hatchet'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A one-handed hatchet.  Makes a great melee weapon, and is useful both for "
"chopping things and for use as a hammer."
msgstr "一柄单手的短斧，是一件不错的近战武器，也可以用于砍柴与捶打。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "electric chainsaw (off)"
msgid_plural "electric chainsaws (off)"
msgstr[0] "电动链锯（关）"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'electric chainsaw (off)', 'str_pl': 'electric
#. chainsaws (off)'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "You turn on the electric chainsaw."
msgstr "你启动了电动链锯。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'electric chainsaw (off)', 'str_pl': 'electric
#. chainsaws (off)'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a lumbering tool moonlighting as weapon of opportunity.  If loaded "
"with batteries, using this item will cause it to turn on, turning it into a "
"very powerful but unwieldy melee weapon."
msgstr "便利的伐木工具，偶尔也作为武器使用。填装电池之后，使用它以将它启动。威力巨大，不过难以掌控。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "electric chainsaw (on)"
msgid_plural "electric chainsaws (on)"
msgstr[0] "电动链锯（开）"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'electric chainsaw (on)', 'str_pl': 'electric
#. chainsaws (on)'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "You turn off the electric chainsaw."
msgstr "你关闭了电动链锯。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'electric chainsaw (on)', 'str_pl': 'electric
#. chainsaws (on)'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"This electric chainsaw is on and making a lot of noise.  Use it to turn it "
"off."
msgstr "电锯已经启动，发出可怕的噪声。激活它来关闭。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "primitive adze"
msgid_plural "primitive adzes"
msgstr[0] "原始锛"

#. ~ Conditional name for {'str': 'primitive adze'} when COMPONENT_ID matches
#. rock
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "stone adze"
msgid_plural "stone adzes"
msgstr[0] "石锛"

#. ~ Conditional name for {'str': 'primitive adze'} when COMPONENT_ID matches
#. ceramic
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "ceramic adze"
msgid_plural "ceramic adzes"
msgstr[0] "陶瓷锛"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'primitive adze'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a stone or ceramic adze, somewhat useful for smoothing wood objects."
msgstr "一个平头石斧或陶瓷斧，可以用来磨平木制物品。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "primitive axe"
msgid_plural "primitive axes"
msgstr[0] "原始斧"

#. ~ Conditional name for {'str': 'primitive axe'} when COMPONENT_ID matches
#. rock
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "stone axe"
msgid_plural "stone axes"
msgstr[0] "石斧"

#. ~ Conditional name for {'str': 'primitive axe'} when COMPONENT_ID matches
#. ceramic
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "ceramic axe"
msgid_plural "ceramic axes"
msgstr[0] "陶瓷斧"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'primitive axe'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a stone with a narrow edge affixed to a stick.  It can chop wood, "
"but requires much more effort than a modern axe."
msgstr "一块固定在棍子上的窄边石头。它勉强能砍木头，但比现代斧头要费劲得多。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "wood saw"
msgid_plural "wood saws"
msgstr[0] "木锯"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wood saw'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "This is a thin saw, useful for cutting through wood objects."
msgstr "一个易损坏的锯子，可以用来锯木头。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "stone chisel"
msgid_plural "stone chisels"
msgstr[0] "石凿"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'stone chisel'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"This is a short stone chisel.  It can be used to engrave on stone, wood, or "
"soft metals."
msgstr "这是一把短石凿。它可以用来在石头、木头或软金属上雕刻。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "primitive tomahawk"
msgid_plural "primitive tomahawks"
msgstr[0] "原始战斧"

#. ~ Conditional name for {'str': 'primitive tomahawk'} when COMPONENT_ID
#. matches rock
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "stone tomahawk"
msgid_plural "stone tomahawks"
msgstr[0] "石制战斧"

#. ~ Conditional name for {'str': 'primitive tomahawk'} when COMPONENT_ID
#. matches ceramic
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "ceramic tomahawk"
msgid_plural "ceramic tomahawks"
msgstr[0] "陶瓷战斧"

#. ~ Conditional name for {'str': 'primitive tomahawk'} when COMPONENT_ID
#. matches bone
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "bone tomahawk"
msgid_plural "bone tomahawks"
msgstr[0] "骨制战斧"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'primitive tomahawk'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A lightweight one-handed combat hatchet typically made of stone or bone, "
"originally used by the Algonquian people.  It makes for a half decent tool "
"and weapon."
msgstr "一种轻便的单手战斧，通常由石头或骨头制成，最初由阿尔冈基人使用。它是一种半成品工具和武器。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "copper tomahawk"
msgid_plural "copper tomahawks"
msgstr[0] "铜制战斧"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'copper tomahawk'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A lightweight one-handed combat hatchet made using basic copper.  Slightly "
"better than stone, though not as historically accurate."
msgstr "一种使用基本铜材制作的轻型单手战斧。比石头略胜一筹，但没有那么符合历史。"

#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "sandpaper"
msgid_plural "sandpapers"
msgstr[0] "砂纸"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'sandpaper'}
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A sheet of cloth or paper with an abrasive material glued to one side, "
"historically glass or sand, modernly aluminum oxide or silicon carbide.  It "
"is commonly used to smooth, roughen, or strip a wooden surface."
msgstr "一种表面粘有研磨材料的布或纸基产品，早期使用玻璃砂或天然砂，现代多用氧化铝或碳化硅。主要用于木材表面的打磨、粗化或剥离处理。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "pallet of wet adobe bricks"
msgid_plural "pallets of wet adobe bricks"
msgstr[0] "装有黏土砖的托盘（湿）"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'pallet of wet adobe bricks', 'str_pl':
#. 'pallets of wet adobe bricks'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "You test the bricks, and they're solid enough to use."
msgstr "你试了试，这块砖似乎已足够结实可以使用。"

#. ~ Use action not_ready_msg for {'str': 'pallet of wet adobe bricks',
#. 'str_pl': 'pallets of wet adobe bricks'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "The bricks are still too damp to bear weight."
msgstr "这块砖还太湿，承受不了重量。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pallet of wet adobe bricks', 'str_pl': 'pallets
#. of wet adobe bricks'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A pallet full of heavy mud bricks which need to dry slowly to be usable."
msgstr "一个装满重泥砖的托盘，需要慢慢干燥才能使用。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "pallet of dry adobe bricks"
msgid_plural "pallets of dry adobe bricks"
msgstr[0] "装有黏土砖的托盘（干）"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pallet of dry adobe bricks', 'str_pl': 'pallets
#. of dry adobe bricks'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A pallet of humble mud bricks that have dried out while you were out risking"
" your life.  Disassemble it to retrieve your frame and building supplies."
msgstr "一堆简陋的泥砖，在你冒着生命危险出去的时候已经干了。拆开它取回你的框架和建筑用品。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "pallet of wet ceramic"
msgid_plural "pallets of wet ceramic"
msgstr[0] "装有陶瓷的托盘（湿）"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str': 'pallet of wet ceramic', 'str_pl': 'pallets of
#. wet ceramic'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "You test the ceramic, and it's the right consistency to use."
msgstr "你试了试，这陶瓷的稠度合适到可以使用。"

#. ~ Use action not_ready_msg for {'str': 'pallet of wet ceramic', 'str_pl':
#. 'pallets of wet ceramic'}.
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "The ceramic is still too damp to be used."
msgstr "这陶瓷还太湿，还无法使用。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pallet of wet ceramic', 'str_pl': 'pallets of
#. wet ceramic'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A pallet full of crushed wet ceramic, which needs to dry slowly to be "
"usable."
msgstr "一个装满湿碎陶瓷的托盘，需要慢慢干燥才能使用。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "pallet of ceramic clay"
msgid_plural "pallets of ceramic clay"
msgstr[0] "装有陶瓷粘土的托盘"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pallet of ceramic clay', 'str_pl': 'pallets of
#. ceramic clay'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A pallet of ceramic clay which is now ready to be made into pottery.  "
"Disassemble it to retrieve your sheet, frame and crafting supplies."
msgstr "一个装满陶瓷粘土的托盘，现在已经可以制成陶器。拆解它以取回你的板材、框架和工艺用品。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "acetylene-gas machine"
msgid_plural "acetylene-gas machines"
msgstr[0] "乙炔制造机"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'acetylene-gas machine'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This bulky device takes water and calcium carbide and yields unpressurised "
"acetylene."
msgstr "这个大型设备接受水和电石，产出常压的乙炔气。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "angle grinder"
msgid_plural "angle grinders"
msgstr[0] "角磨机"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'angle grinder'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This widespread powertool is often used for removing excess material or "
"polishing surfaces."
msgstr "这种广泛的电动工具经常用于去除多余的材料或抛光表面。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "brick kiln"
msgid_plural "brick kilns"
msgstr[0] "便携式砖窑"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'brick kiln'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a portable charcoal-fired kiln.  It is designed for firing bricks, "
"but you could use it to fire anything made of clay."
msgstr "这是一个可移动的砖窑，设计用来烧砖的，但也可以烧任何粘土制品。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "carding paddles"
msgid_plural "pairs of carding paddles"
msgstr[0] "梳棉拨片"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'carding paddles', 'str_pl': 'pairs of carding
#. paddles'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A pair of toothy wooden paddles used to clean fibers for use in textile "
"production."
msgstr "一只有木齿的拨片，通常用于在纺织品生产中清理纤维。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "paint chipper"
msgid_plural "paint chippers"
msgstr[0] "除漆片"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'paint chipper'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "A tool similar to a chisel, designed to remove paint."
msgstr "一个类似凿子的工具，用来移除油漆。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "clamp"
msgid_plural "clamps"
msgstr[0] "夹具"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'clamp'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This clamp is useful for keeping things still, especially if you have "
"several of them."
msgstr "一个能够保持物体静止不动的夹具，特别是当你同时有好几个夹子的时候。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "claw bar"
msgid_plural "claw bars"
msgstr[0] "带爪撬棍"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'claw bar'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a small prying tool with a clawed bend at one end for pulling "
"spikes.  Use it to open locked doors without destroying them or to lift "
"manhole covers.  You could also wield it to bash some heads in."
msgstr "这是一个小型撬棍，一端有一个带爪的弯曲用于拔出铁钉，可以轻易进出别人的家里而不破坏门或者用来开启下水沟井盖，还可以潇洒的敲开丧尸的脑袋。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "concrete mixer"
msgid_plural "concrete mixers"
msgstr[0] "混凝土搅拌器"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'concrete mixer'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A portable concrete mixer.  It is still large and heavy, but it can be "
"operated solo, and runs on batteries.  It also has a heater built in."
msgstr "一台便携式的水泥搅拌机。虽说便携，仍然庞大而笨重，但是它可以单独运行，并只由电池组供电使用。里面也有一个内置的加热器。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "cordless drill"
msgid_plural "cordless drills"
msgstr[0] "无线电钻"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'cordless drill'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a cordless battery-powered drill with a selection of drill bits."
msgstr "这是一把无线电钻，由电池供电，供有一套钻头可供选择。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "distaff and spindle"
msgid_plural "distaves and spindles"
msgstr[0] "纺线杆和纺锤"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'distaff and spindle', 'str_pl': 'distaves and
#. spindles'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A pair of specialized wooden rods used to spin fibers into thread and yarn."
msgstr "一对儿特制的木杆，用来将纤维纺成线。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "electric jackhammer"
msgid_plural "electric jackhammers"
msgstr[0] "电动冲击钻"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'electric jackhammer'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a construction tool for drilling through hard rock or other "
"surfaces.  It runs on a rechargeable cell, optionally compatible with UPS.  "
"Use it to blast a hole in adjacent solid terrain."
msgstr "一种能够钻穿坚硬岩石或其他表面的建筑工具。它使用可充电电池，并可选择与UPS兼容。开启后，可以把附近的地面或者敌人钻出一个大洞来。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "hacksaw"
msgid_plural "hacksaws"
msgstr[0] "钢锯"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'hacksaw'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "This is a sturdy saw, useful for cutting through metal objects."
msgstr "一把坚固的锯子，适合用来切割金属物品。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "wire saw"
msgid_plural "wire saws"
msgstr[0] "钢丝锯"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wire saw'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a flexible saw made from thin wire, with simple handles on either "
"end.  It should suffice for light metal and wood sawing, or for cutting "
"chain-link fences."
msgstr "这是一种由细钢丝制成的灵活锯，两端有简单的把手。它可以满足轻金属和木材的锯切，或用于切割铁丝网。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "hammer"
msgid_plural "hammers"
msgstr[0] "锤子"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'hammer'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a demagnetized steel claw hammer with a wooden grip.  With a hammer,"
" nails, and two by fours in your inventory, you could board up adjacent "
"doors and windows.  It has myriad other uses as well."
msgstr "这是一把消磁的钢制羊角锤，有一个木头手把。使用铁锤、铁钉与木板就能够加固邻近门窗。此外它还有许多其他用途。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "bronze hammer"
msgid_plural "bronze hammers"
msgstr[0] "青铜锤"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bronze hammer'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a bronze claw hammer with a wooden grip, commonly used where sparks "
"from a steel hammer might be a safety hazard.  You could board up adjacent "
"doors and windows, among myriad other uses."
msgstr "这是一把带有木柄的青铜爪锤，通常用于避免使用钢锤可能引发安全风险的场合，如需要封住相邻的门窗等众多用途。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "hand drill"
msgid_plural "hand drills"
msgstr[0] "手摇钻"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'hand drill'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A primitive manual drill with a single drill bit.  It is slow and it will "
"exhaust you quickly."
msgstr "一种有着单一钻头的原始手工钻头。转速相当缓慢，但会迅速耗尽你的精力。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "rubber hose"
msgid_plural "rubber hoses"
msgstr[0] "橡胶软管"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'rubber hose'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a flexible rubber hose.  It could be used for crafting, or siphoning"
" fuel from a vehicle."
msgstr "一根柔软的橡胶软管。可以用来做东西，也可以用来从载具中抽油。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "utility maintenance kit"
msgid_plural "utility maintenance kits"
msgstr[0] "设施维护工具包"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'utility maintenance kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A compact kit for probing, joining, and extending fluid grid connections in "
"buildings."
msgstr "一个紧凑的工具包，用于探测、连接和扩展建筑物内的流体管网。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "bottle jack"
msgid_plural "bottle jacks"
msgstr[0] "瓶式千斤顶"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bottle jack'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "A portable hydraulic bottle jack used for lifting vehicles."
msgstr "便携式液压瓶式千斤顶，用于起重车辆。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "makeshift jack"
msgid_plural "makeshift jacks"
msgstr[0] "简易千斤顶"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'makeshift jack'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A poorly constructed improvised scissor jack used for lifting vehicles if "
"you're brave enough to use it."
msgstr "粗制滥造的简易剪式千斤顶，用于起重车辆，如果你敢用它的话。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "scissor jack"
msgid_plural "scissor jacks"
msgstr[0] "剪式千斤顶"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'scissor jack'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "A compact scissor jack used for lifting vehicles."
msgstr "紧凑的剪式千斤顶，用于起重车辆。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "jackhammer"
msgid_plural "jackhammers"
msgstr[0] "冲击钻"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'jackhammer'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a construction tool for drilling through hard rock or other "
"surfaces.  It runs on gasoline.  Use it (if loaded) to blast a hole in "
"adjacent solid terrain."
msgstr "一种能够钻穿坚硬岩石或其他表面的建筑工具。它靠汽油驱动，开启后，可以把附近的地面或者敌人钻出一个大洞来。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "Auger"
msgid_plural "Augers"
msgstr[0] "螺旋钻"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'Auger'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a construction tool for boring holes in ground.  It runs on "
"gasoline.  For health reasons alone, augers are a worthwhile investment."
msgstr "这是一种用于在地面钻孔的建筑工具。运作消耗汽油。为了你的身体健康着想，你最好试试。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "electric kiln"
msgid_plural "electric kilns"
msgstr[0] "电动窑炉"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'electric kiln'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a portable electric kiln, powered by batteries.  It is designed for "
"firing bricks, but you could use it to fire anything made of clay.  With a "
"little mechanical know-how, you could probably even convert it to run "
"directly off a vehicle's power system."
msgstr ""
"一个使用电池供电的便携式电窑，原版设计用来烧制砖块，但你可以用它来烧制任何用黏土制品。如果会一些机械知识，你甚至可以把它从电池供电改装为车载电源供电。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "gunsmith repair kit"
msgid_plural "gunsmith repair kits"
msgstr[0] "高级枪械修理包"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'gunsmith repair kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a complete toolkit made to repair damaged firearms, disassemble "
"ammunition and manufacture firearm modifications.  Powered by standard "
"batteries, it can tackle any armory work when coupled with a hand press.  It"
" requires 25 charges of battery power per use."
msgstr ""
"一个可用于修复受损枪械、拆解弹药并制造枪械改装件的完整工具包。使用标准电池供电，搭配手动压弹机后可胜任各种枪械作业。每使用一次消耗25单位的电池电量。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "makeshift hammer"
msgid_plural "makeshift hammers"
msgstr[0] "简易锤子"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'makeshift hammer'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a crude hammer made from a piece of metal affixed to a stick.  It "
"functions adequately as a hammer, but really can't compare to a proper one."
msgstr "粗糙的锤子，用一块金属固定在棍子上制成。虽然当锤子是勉强凑合了，但跟正规的还是没得比。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "metal fileset"
msgid_plural "metal filesets"
msgstr[0] "金属锉刀组"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'metal fileset'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"These tools are commonly used to remove small amounts of materials from the "
"surface of metal objects."
msgstr "这种工具通常用于从金属物体表面去除少量的材料。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "metallic smoother"
msgid_plural "metallic smoothers"
msgstr[0] "金属水泥刮刀"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'metallic smoother'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This metallic tool is most often used to smooth concrete, or mortar, in "
"construction projects."
msgstr "这个金属工具通常是用来在建筑时平整混凝土、抹平砂浆或者刮大白的。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json data/mods/MagicalNights/items/tools.json
msgid "misc repair kit"
msgid_plural "misc repair kits"
msgstr[0] "杂项修理包"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'misc repair kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a portable toolkit, consisting of a small carving knife for precise "
"carving of replacement parts from raw materials, a wood saw for more heavy-"
"duty wood cutting, and a patch of soft material for cleaning surfaces.  If "
"supplied with duct tape, it can be used to repair certain items."
msgstr ""
"这是一个便携式工具包，包括用于从原材料中精确替换部件的小型刻刀、用于切割木材的耐用木锯以及用于清洁表面的柔软布条。配合足够的强力胶带，可用于修复部分材质特殊的物品。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json data/mods/MagicalNights/items/tools.json
msgid "makeshift repair kit"
msgid_plural "makeshift repair kits"
msgstr[0] "简易修理工具包"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'makeshift repair kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a portable toolkit, consisting of a primitive knife for carving "
"replacement parts, an adze for more heavy-duty wood cutting, and a patch of "
"soft material for cleaning surfaces.  It can be used to repair certain items"
" if supplied with pitch, though it isn't ideal for complex work."
msgstr ""
"这是一个便携式工具包，包括一把用于雕刻替换零件的原始刀具、一把用于重型木材切割的扁斧，以及一块用于清洁表面的柔软材料。配合沥青使用，它可以修理某些物品，但不适合复杂的工作。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "plastic mold"
msgid_plural "plastic molds"
msgstr[0] "塑料模具"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'plastic mold'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a plastic mold.  It could be shaped and used to craft items made of "
"plastic."
msgstr "一个塑料模具，可以用于塑性并制造塑料制品。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "multi-tool"
msgid_plural "multi-tools"
msgstr[0] "多功能工具"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'multi-tool'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A cleverly designed all-in-one tool which combines several smaller tools "
"into the handles of a pair of pliers."
msgstr "一个将许多小工具整合进钳子握柄造就的多功能工具。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "acetylene torch"
msgid_plural "acetylene torches"
msgstr[0] "乙炔焊炬"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'acetylene torch', 'str_pl': 'acetylene torches'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A compact tool kit intended for welding and cutting metal, this portable "
"oxyacetylene torch includes a torch handle and cutting attachment in an "
"easy-to-carry tote.  It requires connecting to pressurized cylinders of an "
"appropriate welding gas before use.  In addition to its metalworking uses, "
"you can activate it in order to destroy metal barriers."
msgstr ""
"非常紧凑的小巧的工具包，用来焊接和切割金属。这个便携的氧-"
"乙炔焊炬焊炬包含焊炬握柄，切割配件，整体结构非常便携。需要先连接到含有焊接气体的气罐才能使用。因为它的金工用途，你可以激活它开摧毁金属栅栏。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "paint brush"
msgid_plural "paint brushes"
msgstr[0] "油漆刷"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'paint brush', 'str_pl': 'paint brushes'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "A wide brush, suitable for painting walls."
msgstr "一个大刷子，用来给墙刷漆而不是刷牙。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "pickaxe"
msgid_plural "pickaxes"
msgstr[0] "鹤嘴锄"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pickaxe'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a large steel pickaxe, suitable for breaking up hard things or (with"
" enough skill) hard targets.  Strike the earth!"
msgstr "一把钢制大镐头，刨墙砸头两不误。劳动人民一声吼，地球也要抖三抖！"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "debugging prospecting pick"
msgid_plural "debugging prospecting picks"
msgstr[0] "调试用勘探镐"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'debugging prospecting pick'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a medium pickaxe-slash-hammer that could reveal close by ore "
"pockets. This one has an obscene range, for debugging. God save your CPU."
msgstr "这是一把中型镐锤，可以揭示附近的矿藏。这把是调试用的，探测范围大得离谱。愿上帝保佑你的CPU。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "crude prospecting pick"
msgid_plural "crude prospecting picks"
msgstr[0] "粗制勘探镐"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'crude prospecting pick'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a crude hammer-pick used for finding nearby mineral veins. Terrible "
"for anything you're not basically standing on."
msgstr "这是一把粗制的镐锤，用于寻找附近的矿脉。如果你不是直接站在矿脉上，那它就没什么用。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "copper prospecting pick"
msgid_plural "copper prospecting picks"
msgstr[0] "铜制勘探镐"

#. ~ Description for copper prospecting pick
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a copper hammer-pick used for finding nearby mineral veins. Not "
"accurate enough for long range, but works."
msgstr "这是一把铜制镐锤，用于寻找附近的矿脉。远距离勘探不够精确，但还算管用。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "steel prospecting pick"
msgid_plural "steel prospecting picks"
msgstr[0] "钢制勘探镐"

#. ~ Description for steel prospecting pick
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a steel hammer-pick used for finding nearby mineral veins. Can help "
"you sniff out even faint traces of minerals."
msgstr "这是一把钢制镐锤，用于寻找附近的矿脉。它甚至能帮你嗅出最微弱的矿物痕迹。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "pin reamer"
msgid_plural "pin reamers"
msgstr[0] "针铰刀"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pin reamer'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"Handheld pin reamers of this kind are used to enlarge existing holes, or "
"remove any burs and such from them."
msgstr "这种手持式针铰刀用于扩大现有的孔，或从其中移除任何毛刺之类的东西。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "pliers"
msgid_plural "pliers"
msgstr[0] "手钳"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'pliers'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a basic pair of slip-joint pliers, able to handle basic mechanical "
"work and pulling apart some ammunition cartridges.  Anything too complex "
"will require a wrench."
msgstr "这是一把基本的鲤鱼钳，能用来做一些基本的机械和拆解弹药工作，如果你要做更复杂的工作，那就需要一个扳手了。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "electric polisher"
msgid_plural "electric polishers"
msgstr[0] "电动打磨机"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'electric polisher'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"An electric polisher which can be used to buff metal surfaces until they are"
" reflective like a mirror."
msgstr "一台电动打磨机，可以用来打磨金属地面，直到他们像镜子一样亮。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "stone hammer"
msgid_plural "stone hammers"
msgstr[0] "石锤"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'stone hammer'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a rock affixed to a stick, in the crude facsimile of a hammer.  It "
"functions adequately as a hammer, but really can't compare to a proper one."
msgstr "一个插着棒子的岩石，勉强可以做锤子，但山寨的毕竟比不过真的。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "screwdriver"
msgid_plural "screwdrivers"
msgstr[0] "螺丝刀"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'screwdriver'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a Philips-head screwdriver.  It is important for almost all "
"electronics crafting, most mechanics crafting, and has many more uses."
msgstr "一把十字螺丝刀，对制造电子产品和机械十分重要，而且还有许多其他用途。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "screwdriver set"
msgid_plural "screwdriver sets"
msgstr[0] "螺丝刀组"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'screwdriver set'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a set of screwdrivers in several sizes and blade types.  Guaranteed "
"to have the right tools for more precise work."
msgstr "一把有着多种尺寸和形状接口的螺丝刀。保证有正确的工具来进行更精细的工作"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "firearm repair kit"
msgid_plural "firearm repair kits"
msgstr[0] "基础枪械修理包"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'firearm repair kit'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a portable toolkit made to repair damaged firearms.  Powered by "
"standard batteries, it is a vital tool for long-term firearms maintenance.  "
"It requires 100 charges of battery power per use."
msgstr "一个修复受损的枪械的便携式工具包。使用标准电池，它是长期维护枪械的重要工具。每使用一次消耗100单位的电池电量。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "electric soldering iron"
msgid_plural "electric soldering irons"
msgstr[0] "电烙铁"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'electric soldering iron'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a device with a metal tip that can get very hot.  It is necessary "
"for advanced electronics crafting.  You could also use it to cauterize "
"wounds, if you had to."
msgstr "一块可以被烧得很烫的金属板，可以用来制造电子产品，当然也可以用来灼烧伤口。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "alcohol-fueled soldering iron"
msgid_plural "alcohol-fueled soldering irons"
msgstr[0] "酒精燃料电烙铁"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'alcohol-fueled soldering iron'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a device with a metal tip that can get very hot.  It is necessary "
"for advanced electronics crafting.  A metal tip is hold over the burner to "
"create enough heat to solder.  Not as sophisticated as a regular soldering "
"iron."
msgstr "一块可以被烧得很烫的金属板，可以用来制造电子产品。将金属尖端放在燃烧器上，就能产生足够的热量进行焊接。没有普通电烙铁那么复杂。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "toolbox"
msgid_plural "toolboxes"
msgstr[0] "工具箱"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'toolbox', 'str_pl': 'toolboxes'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a stout metal box containing a complete tool kit suitable for most "
"household maintenance and construction activities."
msgstr "这是一个坚固的金属盒子，内含一套完整的工具，适用于大多数家居维护及建设活动。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "workshop toolbox"
msgid_plural "workshop toolboxes"
msgstr[0] "工坊工具箱"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'workshop toolbox', 'str_pl': 'workshop
#. toolboxes'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a stout metal box containing a complete tool kit suitable for most "
"household maintenance and construction activities, as well as additional "
"tools used in workshops for advanced fabrication jobs."
msgstr "这是一个坚固的金属盒子，内含一套完整的工具，适用于大多数家居维护及建设活动，以及在高级制造工作的工坊中作为工具使用。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "arc welder"
msgid_plural "arc welders"
msgstr[0] "电弧焊枪"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'arc welder'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a battery powered tool for welding metal pieces together using an "
"electric arc.  It is an indispensable tool for construction or repair."
msgstr "这是一个电池供电的工具，可以使用电弧将金属部件焊接在一起。这是一个建筑或维修时不可缺少的工具。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "wooden smoother"
msgid_plural "wooden smoothers"
msgstr[0] "木制水泥刮刀"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wooden smoother'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This large makeshift tool is used in smoothing concrete or mortar in "
"construction projects.  You could also use it as an improvised head-basher."
msgstr "这个大型自制工具通常用于在建筑时平整混凝土、抹平砂浆。你也可以拿它削别人的脑袋。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "wool staple"
msgid_plural "wool staples"
msgstr[0] "羊毛纤维"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wool staple'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"The natural cluster of wool fibers.  Could be processed to the felt patches "
"or yarns."
msgstr "一簇天然羊毛纤维。可以加工成毛毡补丁或毛纱。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "X-Acto knife"
msgid_plural "X-Acto knives"
msgstr[0] "美工刀"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'X-Acto knife', 'str_pl': 'X-Acto knives'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a small, sharp knife, designed for making precise cuts for textiles "
"or crafts.  It could cause decent damage, but is difficult to hit things "
"with it.  Its small, sharp blade allows for precision strikes in the hands "
"of the skilled.  It is too small to butcher corpses with."
msgstr ""
"一把小巧且锋利的刀具，用于在制造工艺品和衣物时进行精确切割使用。伤害不错但很难命中敌人。小巧锋利的刀刃在高手手中能够很精确打击对手。但尺寸太小不适合用来屠宰尸体。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "wrench"
msgid_plural "wrenches"
msgstr[0] "扳手"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wrench', 'str_pl': 'wrenches'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is an adjustable crescent wrench.  It could be a decent melee weapon, "
"and is used in many mechanics crafting recipes."
msgstr "一把扳手，能当做武器握在手里，也是许多机械制造必备之物。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "leather hose"
msgid_plural "leather hoses"
msgstr[0] "皮软管"

#. ~ Description for leather hose
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a hose made out of leather.  Watertight and flexiable, it can be "
"used to siphon fuel from a vehicle tank.  However, it's not as elastic a "
"rubber hose."
msgstr "这是一根用皮革制成的软管。防水又轻便，可以从车辆油箱里抽取燃油。然而这一根没有橡胶软管那么有弹性。"

#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "makeshift hand drill"
msgid_plural "makeshift hand drills"
msgstr[0] "简易手摇钻"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'makeshift hand drill'}
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"This is a makeshift manual drill made out of pipe and improvised drill bit."
"  It is very slow and it will exhaust you quickly."
msgstr "一个用铁管和原始手工钻头制成的简易手摇钻。转速非常缓慢，但会迅速耗尽你的精力。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/alternator.json
msgid "vehicle alternator"
msgid_plural "vehicle alternators"
msgstr[0] "车载交流发电机"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/alternator.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/alternator.json
msgid "car alternator"
msgid_plural "car alternators"
msgstr[0] "轿车发电机"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'car alternator'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/alternator.json
msgid "A standard alternator used to power vehicle electrical systems."
msgstr "一个用来给车上的电气系统供能的发电机。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/alternator.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/alternator.json
msgid "motorbike alternator"
msgid_plural "motorbike alternators"
msgstr[0] "摩托车发电机"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'motorbike alternator'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/alternator.json
msgid ""
"A compact lightweight alternator used to power small vehicle electrical "
"systems."
msgstr "一个紧凑轻便的用来带动小型汽车电气系统的发电机。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/alternator.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/alternator.json
msgid "bicycle alternator"
msgid_plural "bicycle alternators"
msgstr[0] "自行车发电机"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bicycle alternator'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/alternator.json
msgid "A very lightweight alternator used to power a bicycle's headlights."
msgstr "一个非常轻便的用来给自行车车灯供能的发电机。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/alternator.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/alternator.json
msgid "truck alternator"
msgid_plural "truck alternators"
msgstr[0] "卡车发电机"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'truck alternator'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/alternator.json
msgid ""
"A larger and more powerful alternator used to power vehicle electrical "
"systems."
msgstr "一个更强大的用来给车上的电气系统供能的大型发电机。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/alternator.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/alternator.json
msgid "7.5kW generator"
msgid_plural "7.5kW generators"
msgstr[0] "7.5KW 发电机"

#. ~ Description for {'str': '7.5kW generator'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/alternator.json
msgid ""
"A bulky but efficient electrical generator designed to be attached to an "
"engine."
msgstr "一台笨重但高效率的发电机，需要连接到载具引擎上。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/animals.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "yoke and harness"
msgid_plural "yokes and harnesses"
msgstr[0] "挽具"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'yoke and harness', 'str_pl': 'yokes and
#. harnesses'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/animals.json
msgid ""
"A bar and harness to attach a creature to a wheeled vehicle, they then "
"should be able to pull it."
msgstr "把动物拴在有轮子的车辆上的一根杆子和挽具，这样动物就可以拉动车子了。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/armor.json
msgid "rebar grate"
msgid_plural "rebar grates"
msgstr[0] "钢筋栅格"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'rebar grate'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/armor.json
msgid ""
"Interlocked sections of rebar that allows for light and effective "
"reinforcement of vehicle sections."
msgstr "一块钢筋焊接而成的栅板，重量不大却可以有效地加固你的车辆。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/armor.json data/json/vehicleparts/armor.json
msgid "shock absorber"
msgid_plural "shock absorbers"
msgstr[0] "减震器"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'shock absorber'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/armor.json
msgid ""
"This makeshift combination of springs and scrap, when attached to a vehicle "
"section, protects that section from impacts.  The springs can absorb a "
"surprising amount of damage."
msgstr "弹簧与废金属制成的简易组件，安装在车辆的某个部位时，可保护该部位免受冲击。弹簧可以吸收大量的伤害。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/balloon.json data/json/vehicleparts/balloons.json
msgid "airship balloon"
msgid_plural "airship balloons"
msgstr[0] "飞艇气囊"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'airship balloon'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/balloon.json
msgid ""
"A big plastic airbag filled with hydrogen gas.  Provides lift if installed "
"on a vehicle, but you'll need a propeller to do anything more than float up "
"and down."
msgstr "一个充满氢气的大型塑料气囊。如果安装在载具上可以提供升力，但你需要一个螺旋桨才能进行升降以外的动作。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json data/json/vehicleparts/battery.json
msgid "car battery"
msgid_plural "car batteries"
msgstr[0] "汽车电池"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'car battery', 'str_pl': 'car batteries'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json
msgid "A 12v lead-acid battery used to power car electrical systems."
msgstr "一个12伏铅酸蓄电池，通常用于一般车辆的电力系统。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json data/json/vehicleparts/battery.json
msgid "motorbike battery"
msgid_plural "motorbike batteries"
msgstr[0] "摩托车电池"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'motorbike battery', 'str_pl': 'motorbike
#. batteries'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json
msgid ""
"A 12v lead-acid battery used to power smaller vehicles' electrical systems."
msgstr "一个12伏铅酸蓄电池，通常用于小型车辆的电力系统。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json
msgid "small motorbike battery"
msgid_plural "small motorbike batteries"
msgstr[0] "小型摩托车电池"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'small motorbike battery', 'str_pl': 'small
#. motorbike batteries'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json
msgid ""
"A miniature 12v lead-acid battery used to power smaller vehicles' electrical"
" systems."
msgstr "一个12伏铅酸蓄电池，通常用于小型车辆的电力系统。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json
msgid "storage battery case"
msgid_plural "storage battery cases"
msgstr[0] "蓄电池箱"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'storage battery case'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json
msgid ""
"An empty case that can hold a storage battery, complete with charging "
"controller chip, connecting wires, and mechanisms to help lift the battery "
"to be mounted into position."
msgstr "一个可以容纳蓄电池的空箱子，配有充电控制器芯片、连接线和帮助将电池安装到位的机构。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json data/json/vehicleparts/battery.json
msgid "very large storage battery"
msgid_plural "very large storage batteries"
msgstr[0] "蓄电池（超大型）"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'very large storage battery', 'str_pl': 'very
#. large storage batteries'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json
msgid ""
"A huge storage battery containing many lithium-ion cells.  Holds a "
"tremendous amount of energy.  Could be installed into a storage battery case"
" for easy removal from a vehicle, or just welded straight in."
msgstr "一个巨型蓄电池，由许多锂离子电池单元拼接而成。可以储存巨大的能量。可被安装到蓄电池箱上，便于快速拆卸，也可以直接焊接在载具上。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json data/json/vehicleparts/battery.json
msgid "medium storage battery"
msgid_plural "medium storage batteries"
msgstr[0] "蓄电池（中型）"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'medium storage battery', 'str_pl': 'medium
#. storage batteries'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json
msgid "A medium storage battery containing multiple lithium-ion cells."
msgstr "一个中型蓄电池，由数个锂离子电池单元拼接而成。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json data/json/vehicleparts/battery.json
msgid "sea scooter battery"
msgid_plural "sea scooter batteries"
msgstr[0] "水下推进器电池"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'sea scooter battery', 'str_pl': 'sea scooter
#. batteries'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json
msgid ""
"A medium storage battery customized to fit specifically inside the hull of a"
" sea scooter. It also weighs less."
msgstr "一种中型蓄电池，经过定制，专门用于安装在水下推进器的外壳内。它的重量也更轻。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json data/json/vehicleparts/battery.json
msgid "small storage battery"
msgid_plural "small storage batteries"
msgstr[0] "蓄电池（小型）"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'small storage battery', 'str_pl': 'small storage
#. batteries'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json
msgid ""
"A small storage battery created with pre-Cataclysm lithium-ion technology.  "
"Useful for crafting."
msgstr "一个小型蓄电池，由大灾变前的锂离子技术制造而成。可以用来制作物品。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json data/json/vehicleparts/battery.json
msgid "large storage battery"
msgid_plural "large storage batteries"
msgstr[0] "蓄电池（大型）"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'large storage battery', 'str_pl': 'large storage
#. batteries'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/battery.json
msgid ""
"A large storage battery containing many lithium-ion cells.  Could be "
"installed into a storage battery case for easy removal from a vehicle, or "
"just welded straight in."
msgstr "一个大型蓄电池，由许多锂离子电池单元拼接而成。可被安装到蓄电池箱上，便于快速拆卸，也可以直接焊接在载具上。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json
msgid "wood boat hull"
msgid_plural "wood boat hulls"
msgstr[0] "木制船壳"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wood boat hull'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json
msgid ""
"A wooden board that keeps the boat afloat.  Add boat hulls to a vehicle "
"until it floats.  Then attach oars or a motor to get the boat to move."
msgstr "一个让船只保持浮力的木板。将其安装在载具上直到它浮在水上。继续添加桨或者引擎来移动船只。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "raft boat hull"
msgid_plural "raft boat hulls"
msgstr[0] "木筏船体"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'raft boat hull'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json
msgid ""
"Logs tied together to make a vehicle float.  Add boat hulls to a vehicle "
"until it floats.  Then attach oars or a motor to get the boat to move."
msgstr "将原木捆绑在一起，使载具漂浮。将船体添加到载具上直到它能浮起来。然后安装船桨或马达来让船移动。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "gas sac buoyancy cell"
msgid_plural "gas sac buoyancy cells"
msgstr[0] "气囊浮力单元"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'gas sac buoyancy cell'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json
msgid ""
"Several bags tied together, filled with hydrogen to provide buoyancy.  Add "
"buoyancy cells to a vehicle until it floats, or install enough to provide "
"lift for an airship."
msgstr "几个捆在一起的袋子，充满了氢气以提供浮力。将浮力单元添加到载具上直到其漂浮，或者安装足够多的数量为飞艇提供升力。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "plastic boat hull"
msgid_plural "plastic boat hulls"
msgstr[0] "塑料船壳"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'plastic boat hull'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json
msgid ""
"A rigid plastic sheet that keeps the boat afloat.  Add boat hulls to a "
"vehicle until it floats.  Then attach oars or a motor to get the boat to "
"move."
msgstr "一个让船只保持浮力的硬质塑料板。将其安装在载具上直到它浮在水上。继续添加桨或者引擎来移动船只。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "carbon fiber boat hull"
msgid_plural "carbon fiber boat hulls"
msgstr[0] "碳纤维船壳"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'carbon fiber boat hull'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json
msgid ""
"A carbon fiber sheet that keeps the boat afloat.  Add boat hulls to a "
"vehicle until it floats.  Then attach oars or a motor to get the boat to "
"move."
msgstr "一个让船只保持浮力的碳纤维板。将其安装在载具上直到它浮在水上。继续添加桨或者引擎来移动船只。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json
msgid "oars"
msgid_plural "oars"
msgstr[0] "桨"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'oars'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json
msgid "Oars for a boat."
msgstr "船桨，严格说是橹。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json
msgid "sail"
msgid_plural "sails"
msgstr[0] "船帆"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'sail'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json
msgid "A small sail and makeshift rigging for a raft."
msgstr "一面小型帆和用于木筏的简易索具。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "large sail"
msgid_plural "large sails"
msgstr[0] "大型帆"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'large sail'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json
msgid ""
"A wooden mast with sails fit for a yacht or sloop, and about as much rigging"
" as a single sailor can handle."
msgstr "一根木制桅杆，挂有适合游艇或单桅小帆船的帆布，并配有足够一名水手操作的缆索和索具。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "inflatable section"
msgid_plural "inflatable section"
msgstr[0] "充气节"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'inflatable section'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json
msgid "An inflatable boat section."
msgstr "充气艇的一截。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "inflatable airbag"
msgid_plural "inflatable airbag"
msgstr[0] "充气气囊"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'inflatable airbag'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json
msgid "An inflatable airbag."
msgstr "一个充气气囊"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "hovercraft impeller"
msgid_plural "hovercraft impeller"
msgstr[0] "气垫船推进器"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'hovercraft impeller'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/boat.json
msgid ""
"An impeller and skirt used by air-cushion-vehicles to float just above the "
"surface of land or water."
msgstr "一种用于气垫车辆的推进器和裙边，使其能够在陆地或水面上方略微悬浮。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/cables.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "jumper cable"
msgid_plural "jumper cables"
msgstr[0] "跨接电缆"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'jumper cable'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/cables.json
msgid ""
"A jumper cable, like you've seen many times before: it's a short multi-"
"stranded copper cable with power leads on either end, whose main purpose is "
"to share power between vehicles, but can also link other electrical systems."
msgstr "正如你所看到的一样，这是跨接电缆：一小段多用铜线，两端各有一个接头，主要用来在载具间传递电力，但也可以用于连接其它电力系统。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/cables.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "heavy duty tow cable"
msgid_plural "heavy duty tow cables"
msgstr[0] "重型牵引索"

#. ~ Description for heavy duty tow cable
#: data/json/items/vehicle/cables.json
msgid ""
"An extremely heavy duty tow cable made from thick steel wire.  If attached "
"to a vehicle, it could be used to pull another vehicle of any weight."
msgstr "一种由粗钢丝制成的非常重的牵引索。如果连接到一辆车上，它可以用来拉动任何重量的另一辆车。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/cables.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "heavy-duty cable"
msgid_plural "heavy-duty cables"
msgstr[0] "重型电缆"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'heavy-duty cable'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/cables.json
msgid ""
"A long, thick, heavy-duty cable with power leads on either end.  It looks "
"like you could use it to hook up two vehicles to each other.  Can also link "
"other electrical systems."
msgstr "一条又粗又长，两端还镀铅的重型电缆。看来你可以用它来连接两部载具，也可以用来连接其它电力系统。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/cables.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "shiny cable"
msgid_plural "shiny cables"
msgstr[0] "圣光电缆"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'shiny cable'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/cables.json
msgid ""
"This is the cable of the gods: 50 meters long, light as a feather and fits "
"in a matchbook.  You're sure this wasn't supposed to exist, and the way it "
"shimmers makes you uneasy."
msgstr ""
"上帝造出来的电缆：50米长，轻如羽毛，卷一卷就能放进火柴盒！你确信这种东西不可能存在，但事实就摆在眼前，它还在微微发光。（注：The Cable God"
" “电缆之神” 是美国佛罗里达州科勒尔斯普林斯地区的一家经营电缆和家庭影院业务的公司）"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json data/json/vehicleparts/cargo.json
msgid "large wire basket"
msgid_plural "large wire baskets"
msgstr[0] "大号铁丝篮"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'large wire basket'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json
msgid "A large wire basket from a shopping cart."
msgstr "购物推车上用的大篮筐。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json data/json/vehicleparts/cargo.json
msgid "bike rack"
msgid_plural "bike racks"
msgstr[0] "摩托车托架"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bike rack'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json
msgid ""
"A collection of pipes, cams, and straps, mounted on the edge of a vehicle "
"and used to support another vehicle for transport.  It must be mounted on a "
"vehicle to be used."
msgstr "一套由各式钢管、凸轮和带子组成的装置，安装在载具边缘，可托起并运输一辆摩托车。它需要安装在载具上使用。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json data/json/vehicleparts/cargo.json
msgid "large folding wire basket"
msgid_plural "large folding wire baskets"
msgstr[0] "大号可折叠铁丝篮"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'large folding wire basket'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json
msgid "A large wire basket from a shopping cart, modified to be foldable."
msgstr "购物推车上用的大篮筐，可以折叠。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json data/json/vehicleparts/cargo.json
msgid "small folding wire basket"
msgid_plural "small folding wire baskets"
msgstr[0] "小号可折叠铁丝篮"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'small folding wire basket'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json
msgid "A simple wire basket.  It is small and foldable."
msgstr "一个造型简单的铁丝篮。体积很小而且可以折叠。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json
msgid "cargo carrier"
msgid_plural "cargo carriers"
msgstr[0] "货物承载器"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'cargo carrier'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json
msgid ""
"A heavy frame outfitted with tie-downs and attachment points for carrying "
"cargo."
msgstr "一个有着运载货物用的绳索和附着点的重型框架。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json
msgid "carbon cargo carrier"
msgid_plural "carbon cargo carriers"
msgstr[0] "碳纤维货物承载器"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'carbon cargo carrier'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy, yet lightweight carbon structure outfitted with tie-downs and "
"attachment points for carrying cargo."
msgstr "一个坚固又轻便，有着运载货物用的绳索和附着点的碳纤维框架。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json data/json/vehicleparts/cargo.json
msgid "floor trunk"
msgid_plural "floor trunks"
msgstr[0] "地板行李箱"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'floor trunk'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json
msgid ""
"A section of flooring with a cargo-space beneath, and a hinged door for "
"access."
msgstr "地板的一部分，下面的空间可以存放货物，通过一扇铰链门存取物品。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json
msgid "livestock carrier"
msgid_plural "livestock carriers"
msgstr[0] "牲畜笼"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'livestock carrier'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json
msgid ""
"A heavy frame outfitted with tie-downs and attachment points for carrying "
"cargo, with additional railings to keep a large animal in place.  It is "
"meant to hold large animals for transport.  Use it on a suitable animal to "
"capture, use it on an empty tile to release."
msgstr ""
"一个有着运载货物用的绳索和附着点的重型框架，额外安装了用于固定大型动物的围栏，可以用来运输大型动物。激活它后选择需要捕获的动物，或者选择空地放出笼中动物。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json data/json/vehicleparts/cargo.json
msgid "mounted spare tire"
msgid_plural "mounted spare tires"
msgstr[0] "备胎托架（有备胎）"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'mounted spare tire'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json
msgid ""
"A spare tire mounted on a carrier rig, ready to be attached to the rear "
"bumper of a vehicle."
msgstr "备用轮胎已装入托架，可以安装在载具的后保险杠上。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json
msgid "animal locker"
msgid_plural "animal lockers"
msgstr[0] "宠物柜"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'animal locker'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json
msgid ""
"A locker used to contain animals safely during transportation if installed "
"properly.  There is room for animal food and other animal care goods.  It is"
" meant to hold medium or smaller animals for transport.  Use it on a "
"suitable animal to capture, use it on an empty tile to release."
msgstr ""
"一个用于安全运输动物的柜子，需要正确安装在载具上使用。内部有足够的空间供宠物活动和进食，可以用来运输中型和小型动物。激活它后选择需要捕获的动物，或者选择空地放出笼中动物。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/controls.json
msgid "camera display"
msgid_plural "camera displays"
msgstr[0] "摄像头显示屏"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'camera display'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/controls.json
msgid "A set of small monitors.  Required to view cameras' output."
msgstr "一组小型显示屏，有了这玩意才能看到摄像头拍了些什么玩意。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/controls.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "security camera"
msgid_plural "security cameras"
msgstr[0] "保安摄像头"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'security camera'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/controls.json
msgid ""
"A security camera you could connect to a display.  Image quality is quite "
"low, but the field of vision is great."
msgstr "一个可以连接显示屏的安防摄像头。视野广阔，但是图像质量很差。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/controls.json
msgid "vehicle controls"
msgid_plural "sets of vehicle controls"
msgstr[0] "载具控制器"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'vehicle controls', 'str_pl': 'sets of vehicle
#. controls'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/controls.json
msgid "A set of various vehicle controls.  Useful for crafting."
msgstr "一整套用于控制载具的装置设备。可以用来制造物品。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/controls.json
msgid "vehicle tracking device"
msgid_plural "vehicle tracking devices"
msgstr[0] "载具追踪装置"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'vehicle tracking device'}
#: data/json/items/vehicle/controls.json
msgid ""
"A vehicle tracking device.  When installed on a vehicle it allows you track "
"the vehicle."
msgstr "一个车辆追踪装置。把它装在车上，就能追踪车辆位置了。"

#: data/json/items/vehicle/controls.json
msgid "rein and tackle"
